{"parentUuid":"fd8ce4a0-3133-428a-b083-b1f90081161a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffxwm4omCR4CjaCSDwHx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3390,"cache_read_input_tokens":115265,"output_tokens":2972,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1140},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2972,"cache_read_input_tokens":115265,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffxwkmTHmkQxs1aEttk3","type":"assistant","uuid":"d810e61c-885c-40fd-af04-04786bffa9bf","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:51:56.264Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"d810e61c-885c-40fd-af04-04786bffa9bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffxwm4omCR4CjaCSDwHx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Time check: it's 13:51.** Submission is 17:00 — you have ~3 hours, not 6. That changes the plan from \"build everything\" to \"**guarantee a demo exists, then upgrade it with real integrations as they land.**\" Replay mode is now core architecture, not insurance. Writing the plan to that reality."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3390,"cache_read_input_tokens":115265,"output_tokens":2972,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1140},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2972,"cache_read_input_tokens":115265,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffxwkmTHmkQxs1aEttk3","type":"assistant","uuid":"749a1a14-beb4-4326-97f7-c712cb32430b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:51:57.646Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"749a1a14-beb4-4326-97f7-c712cb32430b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffxwm4omCR4CjaCSDwHx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013P2xvnjKhUwEsqP25sA9kZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md","content":"# EVENT SCHEMA — the contract\n\nEverything the UI renders is a flat, append-only list of events.\nAgents emit them. The UI replays them. **Nothing else couples the two tracks.**\n\nThis file is frozen. If you need a change, say so in `status/` — do not edit unilaterally.\n\n## Envelope\n\n```ts\ntype Event = {\n  id: string          // \"e001\", monotonically increasing\n  ts: number          // ms offset from run start (NOT wall clock) — replay uses this\n  type: EventType\n  payload: object     // per-type, below\n}\n```\n\nA run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**\n\n## Types\n\n### `alert.raised` — opens the run\n```ts\n{ part: string            // \"MTC20F2085S1RC48BA1\" (the at-risk MPN)\n  partLabel: string       // \"64GB DDR5-4800 RDIMM\"\n  program: string         // \"AI-SRV-G4 — 480 node cluster\"\n  qtyAtRisk: number\n  burnRatePerMin: number  // drives the money counter\n  deadlineLabel: string   // \"Ship date in 11 days\"\n  reason: string          // \"Supplier cut allocation 40%\"\n  plain: string }         // plain-language subtitle — ALWAYS required\n```\n\n### `agent.message`\n```ts\n{ agent: string   // \"sourcing\" | \"engineering\" | \"quality\" | \"market\" | \"intake\"\n  role: string    // \"Sourcing\" — display name\n  text: string }\n```\n\n### `tool.call`\n```ts\n{ callId: string\n  agent: string\n  tool: \"tavily\" | \"moss\" | \"entire\" | \"zoodata\"\n  label: string    // \"Pulling spot pricing\" — human readable\n  status: \"running\" }\n```\n\n### `tool.result`\n```ts\n{ callId: string\n  kind: \"tavily.sources\" | \"moss.matches\" | \"moss.partmatch\" | \"entire.commit\"\n  payload: ...  // see below\n}\n```\n\n- `tavily.sources` → `{ sources: { title, url, snippet }[] }`\n- `moss.matches` → `{ matches: { id, label, score, thumbnail }[], latencyMs: number }`\n- `moss.partmatch` → `{ query: string, equivalents: { mpn, vendor, score, specs }[] , latencyMs: number }`\n- `entire.commit` → `{ commitHash, blameUrl, summary, sessionId }`\n\n> `latencyMs` is rendered prominently. Sub-10ms on-device is a selling point — show it.\n\n### `candidate.added`\n```ts\n{ id, mpn, vendor, specs: Record<string,string>,\n  pricePerUnit: number, leadTimeWeeks: number, source: string }\n```\n\n### `candidate.status`\n```ts\n{ id, status: \"evaluating\" | \"blocked\" | \"approved\" | \"rejected\",\n  reason: string, plain: string }\n```\n\n### `block.raised` — THE RED MOMENT. Render big.\n```ts\n{ agent: \"engineering\", candidateId: string,\n  reason: string,   // \"Not on platform QVL for AI-SRV-G4\"\n  plain: string }   // \"This supplier was never tested on this server. Could take the cluster down.\"\n```\n\n### `counterfeit.flagged` — THE X-FACTOR. Render two images side by side.\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string,\n  imageA: string,   // submitted module label (path or data URI)\n  imageB: string,   // known-good / known-counterfeit reference\n  score: number,    // similarity\n  latencyMs: number,\n  reason: string, plain: string }\n```\n\n### `approval.requested` — UI shows the big Approve button, replay PAUSES here\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string, summary: string, savingsVsBroker?: number }\n```\n\n### `approval.granted`\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string, by: string }\n```\n\n### `po.drafted`\n```ts\n{ poNumber: string, candidateId: string, qty: number, total: number }\n```\n\n### `policy.committed`\n```ts\n{ commitHash: string, blameUrl: string, summary: string, sessionId: string }\n```\n\n### `run.ended`\n```ts\n{ outcomeLabel: string, dollarsSaved: number, minutesElapsed: number }\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n1. **Every event carries a `plain` field where a judge could get lost.** Design is scored on\n   \"user-friendly\". Jargon with a plain-language subtitle = credible. Jargon alone = lost judge.\n2. **`approval.requested` pauses replay** until the presenter clicks. That click is the\n   only human action in the demo and it must feel deliberate.\n3. The UI renders an unknown event type as a neutral card rather than crashing.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3390,"cache_read_input_tokens":115265,"output_tokens":2972,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1140},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2972,"cache_read_input_tokens":115265,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013P2xvnjKhUwEsqP25sA9kZ":{"file_path":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md","content":"# EVENT SCHEMA — the contract\n\nEverything the UI renders is a flat, append-only list of events.\nAgents emit them. The UI replays them. **Nothing else couples the two tracks.**\n\nThis file is frozen. If you need a change, say so in `status/` — do not edit unilaterally.\n\n## Envelope\n\n```ts\ntype Event = {\n  id: string          // \"e001\", monotonically increasing\n  ts: number          // ms offset from run start (NOT wall clock) — replay uses this\n  type: EventType\n  payload: object     // per-type, below\n}\n```\n\nA run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**\n\n## Types\n\n### `alert.raised` — opens the run\n```ts\n{ part: string            // \"MTC20F2085S1RC48BA1\" (the at-risk MPN)\n  partLabel: string       // \"64GB DDR5-4800 RDIMM\"\n  program: string         // \"AI-SRV-G4 — 480 node cluster\"\n  qtyAtRisk: number\n  burnRatePerMin: number  // drives the money counter\n  deadlineLabel: string   // \"Ship date in 11 days\"\n  reason: string          // \"Supplier cut allocation 40%\"\n  plain: string }         // plain-language subtitle — ALWAYS required\n```\n\n### `agent.message`\n```ts\n{ agent: string   // \"sourcing\" | \"engineering\" | \"quality\" | \"market\" | \"intake\"\n  role: string    // \"Sourcing\" — display name\n  text: string }\n```\n\n### `tool.call`\n```ts\n{ callId: string\n  agent: string\n  tool: \"tavily\" | \"moss\" | \"entire\" | \"zoodata\"\n  label: string    // \"Pulling spot pricing\" — human readable\n  status: \"running\" }\n```\n\n### `tool.result`\n```ts\n{ callId: string\n  kind: \"tavily.sources\" | \"moss.matches\" | \"moss.partmatch\" | \"entire.commit\"\n  payload: ...  // see below\n}\n```\n\n- `tavily.sources` → `{ sources: { title, url, snippet }[] }`\n- `moss.matches` → `{ matches: { id, label, score, thumbnail }[], latencyMs: number }`\n- `moss.partmatch` → `{ query: string, equivalents: { mpn, vendor, score, specs }[] , latencyMs: number }`\n- `entire.commit` → `{ commitHash, blameUrl, summary, sessionId }`\n\n> `latencyMs` is rendered prominently. Sub-10ms on-device is a selling point — show it.\n\n### `candidate.added`\n```ts\n{ id, mpn, vendor, specs: Record<string,string>,\n  pricePerUnit: number, leadTimeWeeks: number, source: string }\n```\n\n### `candidate.status`\n```ts\n{ id, status: \"evaluating\" | \"blocked\" | \"approved\" | \"rejected\",\n  reason: string, plain: string }\n```\n\n### `block.raised` — THE RED MOMENT. Render big.\n```ts\n{ agent: \"engineering\", candidateId: string,\n  reason: string,   // \"Not on platform QVL for AI-SRV-G4\"\n  plain: string }   // \"This supplier was never tested on this server. Could take the cluster down.\"\n```\n\n### `counterfeit.flagged` — THE X-FACTOR. Render two images side by side.\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string,\n  imageA: string,   // submitted module label (path or data URI)\n  imageB: string,   // known-good / known-counterfeit reference\n  score: number,    // similarity\n  latencyMs: number,\n  reason: string, plain: string }\n```\n\n### `approval.requested` — UI shows the big Approve button, replay PAUSES here\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string, summary: string, savingsVsBroker?: number }\n```\n\n### `approval.granted`\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string, by: string }\n```\n\n### `po.drafted`\n```ts\n{ poNumber: string, candidateId: string, qty: number, total: number }\n```\n\n### `policy.committed`\n```ts\n{ commitHash: string, blameUrl: string, summary: string, sessionId: string }\n```\n\n### `run.ended`\n```ts\n{ outcomeLabel: string, dollarsSaved: number, minutesElapsed: number }\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n1. **Every event carries a `plain` field where a judge could get lost.** Design is scored on\n   \"user-friendly\". Jargon with a plain-language subtitle = credible. Jargon alone = lost judge.\n2. **`approval.requested` pauses replay** until the presenter clicks. That click is the\n   only human action in the demo and it must feel deliberate.\n3. The UI renders an unknown event type as a neutral card rather than crashing.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffxwkmTHmkQxs1aEttk3","type":"assistant","uuid":"db29eaae-1de4-4eeb-bd1c-3ad6de709d02","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:52:19.810Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
