atacenter memory over optical transceivers. Lower jargon barrier\n  (Design is scored), better physical prop, QVL is a crisp published artifact for the block beat,\n  counterfeit remarking is a textbook problem, real spot pricing exists for Tavily.\n- **13:55** — HBM is the *villain in the backstory*, not the sourced part. No alternates exist\n  for HBM; conventional DDR5 RDIMM substitutes at module level. Keep this distinction precise —\n  someone in the audience will know.\n- **13:58** — Replay-first architecture. UI consumes an event list; live vs. replay is invisible\n  to it. Guarantees a demo exists by 15:15 regardless of integration state.\n- **13:58** — Single screen. No nav, no auth, no settings.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1,"newLines":7,"lines":[" # LINEDOWN — milestone tracker"," "," **Event:** AI Commerce Gallery, Walt Disney Family Museum — 3 Oct 2026","-**Submission:** 17:00 · **Presentations:** 18:00 · **Plan written:** 13:51 → **~3h650 of build time**","+**Submission:** 17:00 · **Presentations:** 18:00 · **Plan written:** 13:51 → **~3h of build time**"," "," **Product:** LINEDOWN — the sourcing desk that keeps the line running."," **Segment:** Datacenter memory. **Buyer:** server ODM / systems integrator."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cbaa1575-a42b-4b0c-8760-6fee579105ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"940c68b5-4737-42ca-ad22-1c1e941317ca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffy3cR54d4wLyz1VVSfW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CZrAkzGk5ni8Qxc2iGXfZz","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Moss multimodal go/no-go spike","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"moss-spike","prompt":"You are the MOSS track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline is 17:00 today; your GO/NO-GO is due by 14:20. SPEED OVER COMPLETENESS.\n\nRead MILESTONES.md and docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md first.\n\nMoss (moss.dev, github.com/usemoss, docs.moss.dev) is an on-device semantic search runtime: moss-minilm, 32MB, claims text + image + audio embedding, hybrid vector+keyword, <10ms @ 100K docs. Hackathon code: GALLERYHACKS.\n\nYOUR ONE CRITICAL QUESTION, answer it within 25 minutes: **does the Moss SDK actually expose image embedding/indexing today, or is it text-only in practice?** The entire demo's X-Factor depends on matching a photographed DRAM module label against reference markings.\n\nSteps:\n1. Fetch docs.moss.dev and the usemoss GitHub org. Find the real SDK surface (install, auth, index creation, query, and CRUCIALLY whether documents can be images).\n2. Write the answer to status/moss.md IMMEDIATELY once known, as the first line: \"GO\" or \"NO-GO: <reason>\".\n3. Then write working code in spikes/moss/ for whichever path is real:\n   - Two functions: `findEquivalents(partNumber)` — cross-vendor DDR5 RDIMM part-number/spec matching; and `matchMarking(imagePathOrText)` — returns top-k matches with similarity scores AND measured latency in ms.\n   - If image embedding is NOT available, fall back to text matching over DRAM top-marking strings, lot codes and date codes. Same demo beat, less visual. Say so clearly.\n4. Both functions must return shapes that map onto `moss.partmatch` and `moss.matches` in docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md, including `latencyMs` — latency is rendered prominently on stage.\n5. Include a runnable `spikes/moss/demo.py` (or .ts) that indexes a handful of fixtures and prints results, so it can be verified in one command.\n\nThe user has API credits for all sponsors but keys are NOT in this environment — write code that reads keys from env vars (document which ones in status/moss.md) and make the fixtures self-contained so it can be run the moment keys are exported.\n\nKeep status/moss.md updated with: GO/NO-GO, exact install command, env var names, the call signatures you verified, and any gotcha that would cost someone 20 minutes. Do not edit any file outside spikes/moss/ and status/moss.md."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"output_tokens":6008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":156},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CZrAkzGk5ni8Qxc2iGXfZz":{"description":"Moss multimodal go/no-go spike","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"moss-spike","prompt":"You are the MOSS track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline is 17:00 today; your GO/NO-GO is due by 14:20. SPEED OVER COMPLETENESS.\n\nRead MILESTONES.md and docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md first.\n\nMoss (moss.dev, github.com/usemoss, docs.moss.dev) is an on-device semantic search runtime: moss-minilm, 32MB, claims text + image + audio embedding, hybrid vector+keyword, <10ms @ 100K docs. Hackathon code: GALLERYHACKS.\n\nYOUR ONE CRITICAL QUESTION, answer it within 25 minutes: **does the Moss SDK actually expose image embedding/indexing today, or is it text-only in practice?** The entire demo's X-Factor depends on matching a photographed DRAM module label against reference markings.\n\nSteps:\n1. Fetch docs.moss.dev and the usemoss GitHub org. Find the real SDK surface (install, auth, index creation, query, and CRUCIALLY whether documents can be images).\n2. Write the answer to status/moss.md IMMEDIATELY once known, as the first line: \"GO\" or \"NO-GO: <reason>\".\n3. Then write working code in spikes/moss/ for whichever path is real:\n   - Two functions: `findEquivalents(partNumber)` — cross-vendor DDR5 RDIMM part-number/spec matching; and `matchMarking(imagePathOrText)` — returns top-k matches with similarity scores AND measured latency in ms.\n   - If image embedding is NOT available, fall back to text matching over DRAM top-marking strings, lot codes and date codes. Same demo beat, less visual. Say so clearly.\n4. Both functions must return shapes that map onto `moss.partmatch` and `moss.matches` in docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md, including `latencyMs` — latency is rendered prominently on stage.\n5. Include a runnable `spikes/moss/demo.py` (or .ts) that indexes a handful of fixtures and prints results, so it can be verified in one command.\n\nThe user has API credits for all sponsors but keys are NOT in this environment — write code that reads keys from env vars (document which ones in status/moss.md) and make the fixtures self-contained so it can be run the moment keys are exported.\n\nKeep status/moss.md updated with: GO/NO-GO, exact install command, env var names, the call signatures you verified, and any gotcha that would cost someone 20 minutes. Do not edit any file outside spikes/moss/ and status/moss.md."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cffy3begrUqQvHzRvHMkB","type":"assistant","uuid":"