d vector+keyword, <10ms @ 100K docs. Hackathon code: GALLERYHACKS.\n\nYOUR ONE CRITICAL QUESTION, answer it within 25 minutes: **does the Moss SDK actually expose image embedding/indexing today, or is it text-only in practice?** The entire demo's X-Factor depends on matching a photographed DRAM module label against reference markings.\n\nSteps:\n1. Fetch docs.moss.dev and the usemoss GitHub org. Find the real SDK surface (install, auth, index creation, query, and CRUCIALLY whether documents can be images).\n2. Write the answer to status/moss.md IMMEDIATELY once known, as the first line: \"GO\" or \"NO-GO: <reason>\".\n3. Then write working code in spikes/moss/ for whichever path is real:\n   - Two functions: `findEquivalents(partNumber)` — cross-vendor DDR5 RDIMM part-number/spec matching; and `matchMarking(imagePathOrText)` — returns top-k matches with similarity scores AND measured latency in ms.\n   - If image embedding is NOT available, fall back to text matching over DRAM top-marking strings, lot codes and date codes. Same demo beat, less visual. Say so clearly.\n4. Both functions must return shapes that map onto `moss.partmatch` and `moss.matches` in docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md, including `latencyMs` — latency is rendered prominently on stage.\n5. Include a runnable `spikes/moss/demo.py` (or .ts) that indexes a handful of fixtures and prints results, so it can be verified in one command.\n\nThe user has API credits for all sponsors but keys are NOT in this environment — write code that reads keys from env vars (document which ones in status/moss.md) and make the fixtures self-contained so it can be run the moment keys are exported.\n\nKeep status/moss.md updated with: GO/NO-GO, exact install command, env var names, the call signatures you verified, and any gotcha that would cost someone 20 minutes. Do not edit any file outside spikes/moss/ and status/moss.md.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/ab2d6c1d0079879cb.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"71aac42d-3a82-46e3-8d95-c6639aa80147","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"b26624b1-ced1-4560-a4df-f821f5861778","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffy3cR54d4wLyz1VVSfW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011AohVHJ8Z7nBfvHu2o4PWn","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Sponsor SDK integration recon","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"recon","prompt":"You are the RECON track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline 17:00 today; your deliverable is due 14:25. You are on the critical path — the AGENTS track is blocked until you deliver.\n\nRead MILESTONES.md first.\n\nProduce docs/INTEGRATION.md: exact, copy-pasteable integration notes for five sponsor platforms. For EACH one: install command, auth/env var names, the 3-5 API calls we actually need with real signatures, one minimal working snippet, and any gotcha that would cost 20 minutes.\n\n1. **ZooWork** (zoowork.ai/docs) — THE most important, there is a \"Best Use of ZooWork\" prize. Install is `npx skills add SerendipityOneInc/zoowork-sdk-skills` (needs Node 22.20+). Also see github.com/SerendipityOneInc/zoowork-sdk-typescript and zoowork-agents-docs. Primitives are Agent (model, instructions, tools, skills) → Session (one conversation) → Events (streamed back: messages, tool activity, replies). Nail: how to define an agent, how to start a session, how to stream events, how to attach tools/MCP servers, and how model IDs are specified (check whether they need provider prefixes).\n2. **Tavily** — /search, /extract, /map, /crawl, /research. We need search + extract. Note credit costs.\n3. **Entire** (entire.io) — CLI install is `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash`. We need: how to capture an agent session, how to commit with the session attached, and the exact command that produces a `blame` view showing the prompt behind a line. Find whether there's a shareable blame URL.\n4. **BAND** — multi-agent \"rooms\" where agents from different parties collaborate, including across company lines, with Critic agents that can block. Find the actual SDK/API. Start from github.com/Band-AI and search for their docs. If you cannot find a real API in 15 minutes, say so plainly in status/recon.md and describe the smallest credible local stand-in (a room orchestrator with typed turn-taking and a blocking Critic) — do NOT burn an hour hunting.\n5. **Moss** — skip, another agent owns it. Just note it is covered.\n\nWrite progress to status/recon.md as you go: a line per sponsor, marked VERIFIED (you read real docs) or UNVERIFIED (inferred). Honesty matters more than completeness here — an UNVERIFIED label saves someone a wasted hour, a confident guess costs them one.\n\nDo not edit files outside docs/INTEGRATION.md and status/recon.md."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"output_tokens":6008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":156},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011AohVHJ8Z7nBfvHu2o4PWn":{"description":"Sponsor SDK integration recon","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"recon","prompt":"You are the RECON track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline 17:00 today; your deliverable is due 14:25. You are on the critical path — the AGENTS track is blocked until you deliver.\n\nRead MILESTONES.m