{"parentUuid":"a61a3d4a-de08-4c92-80f6-69504dc9edd9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffy3cR54d4wLyz1VVSfW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015FSA3VDGHphGvd8j9f52Mx","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Seed data and mock event log","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"data","prompt":"You are the DATA track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline 17:00 today; your deliverables are due 14:35. The UI track is blocked on your mock event log — ship that FIRST.\n\nRead MILESTONES.md and docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md carefully. The schema is frozen; conform to it exactly.\n\nScenario: a server ODM building an AI training cluster (\"AI-SRV-G4\", 480 nodes). Their qualified 64GB DDR5-4800 RDIMM just had its allocation cut 40%. The sourcing desk must find a qualified alternate before the ship date.\n\nDeliver, in priority order:\n\n1. **data/mock-events.json** — a complete, replayable 7-beat run conforming to docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md. The 7 beats are listed in MILESTONES.md. Pace it over ~150 seconds of `ts` offsets so it plays as a 2.5-minute demo. This is your most important artifact. Make the dialogue between agents sound like real procurement people, not chatbots — terse, specific, slightly adversarial.\n2. **data/bom.json** — ~20 BOM lines for the program, with the at-risk RDIMM flagged.\n3. **data/candidates.json** — 4 alternate RDIMM modules from different vendors. Design them so:\n   - one is cheapest but NOT on the platform QVL → Engineering blocks it (beat 4)\n   - one is a broker/grey-market offer with a suspiciously good price → counterfeit catch (beat 5)\n   - one is qualified, available, slightly more expensive → the approved winner (beat 6)\n   - one is qualified but lead time is too long → rejected on schedule\n4. **data/qvl.json** — a platform qualified-vendor list for AI-SRV-G4 that makes the block decision a real lookup, not a hardcoded string.\n5. **data/markings/** — fixtures for the counterfeit beat: reference top-marking strings/lot codes for genuine modules plus one remarked/counterfeit example. Include plain .txt or .json marking data so this works even if image embedding is unavailable. If you can generate simple placeholder label images (PIL or SVG), do so — but text fixtures first.\n\nCRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:\n- Use **realistic** part numbers, vendors, speeds, capacities and lead times for server DDR5 RDIMMs. Someone in the audience will know this market. Precision here buys credibility.\n- Be precise about module-level vs die-level: we are sourcing an alternate MODULE, not substituting DRAM die. Never imply otherwise.\n- EVERY event needs its `plain` field — a plain-language subtitle for a judge who does not know what a QVL is. This is a scored criterion. \"Not on the QVL\" → \"This supplier was never tested on this server. Could take the cluster down.\"\n- Do not use real current prices as fact; mark pricing as illustrative in a comment field. The AGENTS track may replace them with live Tavily data later.\n\nWrite progress to status/data.md. Do not edit files outside data/ and status/data.md."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"output_tokens":6008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":156},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015FSA3VDGHphGvd8j9f52Mx":{"description":"Seed data and mock event log","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"data","prompt":"You are the DATA track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline 17:00 today; your deliverables are due 14:35. The UI track is blocked on your mock event log — ship that FIRST.\n\nRead MILESTONES.md and docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md carefully. The schema is frozen; conform to it exactly.\n\nScenario: a server ODM building an AI training cluster (\"AI-SRV-G4\", 480 nodes). Their qualified 64GB DDR5-4800 RDIMM just had its allocation cut 40%. The sourcing desk must find a qualified alternate before the ship date.\n\nDeliver, in priority order:\n\n1. **data/mock-events.json** — a complete, replayable 7-beat run conforming to docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md. The 7 beats are listed in MILESTONES.md. Pace it over ~150 seconds of `ts` offsets so it plays as a 2.5-minute demo. This is your most important artifact. Make the dialogue between agents sound like real procurement people, not chatbots — terse, specific, slightly adversarial.\n2. **data/bom.json** — ~20 BOM lines for the program, with the at-risk RDIMM flagged.\n3. **data/candidates.json** — 4 alternate RDIMM modules from different vendors. Design them so:\n   - one is cheapest but NOT on the platform QVL → Engineering blocks it (beat 4)\n   - one is a broker/grey-market offer with a suspiciously good price → counterfeit catch (beat 5)\n   - one is qualified, available, slightly more expensive → the approved winner (beat 6)\n   - one is qualified but lead time is too long → rejected on schedule\n4. **data/qvl.json** — a platform qualified-vendor list for AI-SRV-G4 that makes the block decision a real lookup, not a hardcoded string.\n5. **data/markings/** — fixtures for the counterfeit beat: reference top-marking strings/lot codes for genuine modules plus one remarked/counterfeit example. Include plain .txt or .json marking data so this works even if image embedding is unavailable. If you can generate simple placeholder label images (PIL or SVG), do so — but text fixtures first.\n\nCRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:\n- Use **realistic** part numbers, vendors, speeds, capacities and lead times for server DDR5 RDIMMs. Someone in the audience will know this market. Precision here buys credibility.\n- Be precise about module-level vs die-level: we are sourcing an alternate MODULE, not substituting DRAM die. Never imply otherwise.\n- EVERY event needs its `plain` field — a plain-language subtitle for a judge who does not know what a QVL is. This is a scored criterion. \"Not on the QVL\" → \"This supplier was never tested on this server. Could take the cluster down.\"\n- Do not use real current prices as fact; mark pricing as illustrative in a comment field. The AGENTS track may replace them with live Tavily data later.\n\nWrite progress to status/data.md. Do not edit files outside data/ and status/data.md."}},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cffy3begrUqQvHzRvHMkB","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba8237b0-840e-46eb-89b3-ea598ba672a5","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:53:45.098Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
