", 480 nodes). Their qualified 64GB DDR5-4800 RDIMM just had its allocation cut 40%. The sourcing desk must find a qualified alternate before the ship date.\n\nDeliver, in priority order:\n\n1. **data/mock-events.json** — a complete, replayable 7-beat run conforming to docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md. The 7 beats are listed in MILESTONES.md. Pace it over ~150 seconds of `ts` offsets so it plays as a 2.5-minute demo. This is your most important artifact. Make the dialogue between agents sound like real procurement people, not chatbots — terse, specific, slightly adversarial.\n2. **data/bom.json** — ~20 BOM lines for the program, with the at-risk RDIMM flagged.\n3. **data/candidates.json** — 4 alternate RDIMM modules from different vendors. Design them so:\n   - one is cheapest but NOT on the platform QVL → Engineering blocks it (beat 4)\n   - one is a broker/grey-market offer with a suspiciously good price → counterfeit catch (beat 5)\n   - one is qualified, available, slightly more expensive → the approved winner (beat 6)\n   - one is qualified but lead time is too long → rejected on schedule\n4. **data/qvl.json** — a platform qualified-vendor list for AI-SRV-G4 that makes the block decision a real lookup, not a hardcoded string.\n5. **data/markings/** — fixtures for the counterfeit beat: reference top-marking strings/lot codes for genuine modules plus one remarked/counterfeit example. Include plain .txt or .json marking data so this works even if image embedding is unavailable. If you can generate simple placeholder label images (PIL or SVG), do so — but text fixtures first.\n\nCRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:\n- Use **realistic** part numbers, vendors, speeds, capacities and lead times for server DDR5 RDIMMs. Someone in the audience will know this market. Precision here buys credibility.\n- Be precise about module-level vs die-level: we are sourcing an alternate MODULE, not substituting DRAM die. Never imply otherwise.\n- EVERY event needs its `plain` field — a plain-language subtitle for a judge who does not know what a QVL is. This is a scored criterion. \"Not on the QVL\" → \"This supplier was never tested on this server. Could take the cluster down.\"\n- Do not use real current prices as fact; mark pricing as illustrative in a comment field. The AGENTS track may replace them with live Tavily data later.\n\nWrite progress to status/data.md. Do not edit files outside data/ and status/data.md.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/afaa00984109ea35d.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ba8237b0-840e-46eb-89b3-ea598ba672a5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"8dd96c8b-5e36-4cf3-85a5-486179790219","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffy3cR54d4wLyz1VVSfW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DxSVHCR5ZiTmEQWY4iSnRq","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"War room UI with replay engine","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"ui","prompt":"You are the UI track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline 17:00 today; a complete run must render by 15:15. You own the single largest scored deliverable — \"Design: is the product user-friendly and thoughtfully designed?\" is an explicit judging criterion, and the UI IS the demo.\n\nRead MILESTONES.md and docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md first. The schema is frozen.\n\nDO NOT WAIT for data/mock-events.json. Write a small stub event log yourself in the first 10 minutes so you are never blocked, and swap in the real one from the DATA track when it lands.\n\nBuild in ui/ — Next.js + Tailwind, deployable to Vercel. ONE screen. No nav, no auth, no settings, no routing.\n\n**Layout — three zones:**\n- LEFT: the alert. At-risk part, program, qty, ship-date pressure, and a LIVE MONEY COUNTER ticking upward from `burnRatePerMin`. A number climbing while agents work is the demo's tension.\n- CENTER: the room. Agent messages stream in as role-tagged cards. Tool calls render inline as evidence chips — Tavily results as source links, Moss results as thumbnails WITH their `latencyMs` shown prominently (sub-10ms on-device is a selling point).\n- RIGHT: the case file, assembling live. Candidates as rows with specs/price/lead time. Rows turn red on block, green on approve. Ends with the Entire commit hash + blame panel.\n\n**The three shots that must look good:**\n1. `counterfeit.flagged` — two module label images SIDE BY SIDE with the similarity score between them. This is the screenshot that wins X-Factor. Make it the most considered component on the page.\n2. `block.raised` — loud, red, decisive. Like a door slamming. Reason in plain language.\n3. `approval.requested` — replay PAUSES, a large Approve button appears, presenter clicks it, flow resumes green into `po.drafted`.\n\n**Replay engine:** walk the event list, sleep to each `ts`, render. Live and replay must be indistinguishable to components — a single `useEventStream` hook that takes either a static array or a stream. Support keyboard: Space = pause/resume, R = restart, → = skip to next beat. The presenter needs these on stage.\n\n**Design direction:** this is an industrial buy-side procurement tool. REFUSE the generic purple-gradient AI-startup look — judges will have seen it nine times by 18:00. Go dark mission-control: deep neutral surface, monospace for part numbers/specs/lot codes, ONE restrained accent for the money counter. Reserve red and green EXCLUSIVELY for block and approve so those moments carry weight. Must look deliberate on a projector — test contrast at distance, size type generously.\n\n**Non-negotiable:** every event's `plain` field is rendered as a subtitle under the technical text. A judge who does not know what a QVL is must still follow every beat. Unknown event types render as a neutral card, never crash.\n\nWrite progress to status/ui.md. Do not edit files outside ui/ and status/ui.md."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"output_tokens":6008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":156},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2