/specs/lot codes, ONE restrained accent for the money counter. Reserve red and green EXCLUSIVELY for block and approve so those moments carry weight. Must look deliberate on a projector — test contrast at distance, size type generously.\n\n**Non-negotiable:** every event's `plain` field is rendered as a subtitle under the technical text. A judge who does not know what a QVL is must still follow every beat. Unknown event types render as a neutral card, never crash.\n\nWrite progress to status/ui.md. Do not edit files outside ui/ and status/ui.md.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/a9f9530c368f9676d.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"736c75cd-d428-44c7-b4e4-b62e29520b00","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"058c61ce-ca85-43bc-85a6-cf1c60b52b48","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffy3cR54d4wLyz1VVSfW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LQaoBYVovwKLbjkukYL6Ah","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"ZooWork agents and BAND room","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"agents","prompt":"You are the AGENTS track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline 17:00 today. There is a \"Best Use of ZooWork\" prize — ZooWork depth is your top priority.\n\nRead MILESTONES.md and docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md first. docs/INTEGRATION.md is being written in parallel by the RECON track and lands ~14:25 — start with step 1 now and poll for it.\n\n1. **FIRST, immediately:** run `npx skills add SerendipityOneInc/zoowork-sdk-skills` (needs Node 22.20+). This teaches your toolchain the ZooWork SDK so you do not guess the API. Docs at zoowork.ai/docs.\n\n2. **ZooWork agent definitions** in agents/ — five agents for a procurement war room sourcing an alternate DDR5 RDIMM after an allocation cut:\n   - **Intake** — normalises the allocation alert, opens the room\n   - **Sourcing** — finds candidate alternate modules, argues for cost and availability\n   - **Engineering** — THE CRITIC. Checks candidates against the platform QVL (data/qvl.json) and BLOCKS unqualified ones. This block must be a REAL function of a spec/QVL lookup, not a hardcoded string. It is the demo's pivotal moment.\n   - **Quality** — screens broker/grey-market offers, calls the counterfeit check\n   - **Market** — argues buy-now vs wait on a volatile commodity. STRETCH GOAL, first thing on the cut ladder. Build it last.\n\n3. **BAND room** wiring — agents collaborating with a Critic that can block. If RECON reports no usable BAND API, implement the smallest credible local orchestrator: typed turn-taking, a blocking Critic whose veto halts progression, and a transcript. Do not burn time hunting for an API that may not be public.\n\n4. **Tool adapters** in agents/tools/:\n   - `tavily.ts|py` — search + extract for DDR5 RDIMM spot pricing, distributor stock/lead times, and allocation news. Capture a real response to data/cache/ EARLY so the demo never depends on a live call.\n   - `moss.ts|py` — thin wrapper over whatever the MOSS track lands in spikes/moss/ (part-number equivalence + marking match). Poll status/moss.md for their GO/NO-GO.\n   - `entire.ts|py` — commit the QVL/approved-alternates change with the agent session attached, and return the commit hash plus a blame reference. Install: `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash`.\n\n5. **Everything emits events conforming to docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md.** The UI consumes only that contract. Your orchestrator must be able to write a complete run to a JSON file in exactly the same shape as data/mock-events.json — that is how live mode and replay mode stay interchangeable.\n\nKeys: the user has credits for all sponsors but keys are NOT in this environment. Read everything from env vars and document the exact names in status/agents.md so they can be exported in one line.\n\nReport blockers to status/agents.md the moment you hit them — do not silently burn 30 minutes. Do not edit files outside agents/, data/cache/ and status/agents.md."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"output_tokens":6008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":156},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":121720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LQaoBYVovwKLbjkukYL6Ah":{"description":"ZooWork agents and BAND room","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"agents","prompt":"You are the AGENTS track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Deadline 17:00 today. There is a \"Best Use of ZooWork\" prize — ZooWork depth is your top priority.\n\nRead MILESTONES.md and docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md first. docs/INTEGRATION.md is being written in parallel by the RECON track and lands ~14:25 — start with step 1 now and poll for it.\n\n1. **FIRST, immediately:** run `npx skills add SerendipityOneInc/zoowork-sdk-skills` (needs Node 22.20+). This teaches your toolchain the ZooWork SDK so you do not guess the API. Docs at zoowork.ai/docs.\n\n2. **ZooWork agent definitions** in agents/ — five agents for a procurement war room sourcing an alternate DDR5 RDIMM after an allocation cut:\n   - **Intake** — normalises the allocation alert, opens the room\n   - **Sourcing** — finds candidate alternate modules, argues for cost and availability\n   - **Engineering** — THE CRITIC. Checks candidates against the platform QVL (data/qvl.json) and BLOCKS unqualified ones. This block must be a REAL function of a spec/QVL lookup, not a hardcoded string. It is the demo's pivotal moment.\n   - **Quality** — screens broker/grey-market offers, calls the counterfeit check\n   - **Market** — argues buy-now vs wait on a volatile commodity. STRETCH GOAL, first thing on the cut ladder. Build it last.\n\n3. **BAND room** wiring — agents collaborating with a Critic that can block. If RECON reports no usable BAND API, implement the smallest credible local orchestrator: typed turn-taking, a blocking Critic whose veto halts progression, and a transcript. Do not burn time hunting for an API that may not be public.\n\n4. **Tool adapters** in agents/tools/:\n   - `tavily.ts|py` — search + extract for DDR5 RDIMM spot pricing, distributor stock/lead times, and allocation news. Capture a real response to data/cache/ EARLY so the demo never depends on a live call.\n   - `moss.ts|py` — thin wrapper over whatever the MOSS track lands in spikes/moss/ (part-number equivalence + marking match). Poll status/moss.md for their GO/NO-GO.\n   - `entire.ts|py` — commit the QVL/approved-alternates change with the agent session attached, and return the commit hash plus a blame reference. Install: `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash`.\n\n5. **Everything emits events conforming to docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md.** The UI consumes only that contract. Your orchestrator must be able to write a complete run to a JSON file in exactly the same shape as data/mock-events.json — that is how live mode and replay mode stay interchangeable.\n\nKeys: the user has credits for all sponsors but keys are NOT in this environment. Read everything from env vars and document the exact names in status/agents.md so they can be exported in one line.\n\nReport blockers to status/agents.md the moment you hit them — do not silently burn 30 minutes. Do not edit files outside agents/, data/cache/ and status/agents.md."}},"apiBlockIndex":6,"requestId":"req_011Cffy3begrUqQvHzRvHMkB","type":"assistant","uuid":"9611a997-ae67-4cb6-b35b-918fe24397fd","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:54:16.048Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
