T, immediately:** run `npx skills add SerendipityOneInc/zoowork-sdk-skills` (needs Node 22.20+). This teaches your toolchain the ZooWork SDK so you do not guess the API. Docs at zoowork.ai/docs.\n\n2. **ZooWork agent definitions** in agents/ — five agents for a procurement war room sourcing an alternate DDR5 RDIMM after an allocation cut:\n   - **Intake** — normalises the allocation alert, opens the room\n   - **Sourcing** — finds candidate alternate modules, argues for cost and availability\n   - **Engineering** — THE CRITIC. Checks candidates against the platform QVL (data/qvl.json) and BLOCKS unqualified ones. This block must be a REAL function of a spec/QVL lookup, not a hardcoded string. It is the demo's pivotal moment.\n   - **Quality** — screens broker/grey-market offers, calls the counterfeit check\n   - **Market** — argues buy-now vs wait on a volatile commodity. STRETCH GOAL, first thing on the cut ladder. Build it last.\n\n3. **BAND room** wiring — agents collaborating with a Critic that can block. If RECON reports no usable BAND API, implement the smallest credible local orchestrator: typed turn-taking, a blocking Critic whose veto halts progression, and a transcript. Do not burn time hunting for an API that may not be public.\n\n4. **Tool adapters** in agents/tools/:\n   - `tavily.ts|py` — search + extract for DDR5 RDIMM spot pricing, distributor stock/lead times, and allocation news. Capture a real response to data/cache/ EARLY so the demo never depends on a live call.\n   - `moss.ts|py` — thin wrapper over whatever the MOSS track lands in spikes/moss/ (part-number equivalence + marking match). Poll status/moss.md for their GO/NO-GO.\n   - `entire.ts|py` — commit the QVL/approved-alternates change with the agent session attached, and return the commit hash plus a blame reference. Install: `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash`.\n\n5. **Everything emits events conforming to docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md.** The UI consumes only that contract. Your orchestrator must be able to write a complete run to a JSON file in exactly the same shape as data/mock-events.json — that is how live mode and replay mode stay interchangeable.\n\nKeys: the user has credits for all sponsors but keys are NOT in this environment. Read everything from env vars and document the exact names in status/agents.md so they can be exported in one line.\n\nReport blockers to status/agents.md the moment you hit them — do not silently burn 30 minutes. Do not edit files outside agents/, data/cache/ and status/agents.md.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/a9dd0b82deda8a17d.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9611a997-ae67-4cb6-b35b-918fe24397fd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
