{"parentUuid":"ef1c87ad-270f-44f8-ba42-171abc10d427","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffyfwjvPRJdfVfD7FLQM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Open in VSCode now: [.env](.env)\n\nTwo things worth knowing:\n\n- **My earlier \"opened\" was wrong** — `code` isn't on your PATH, so that command fell through to `open -e` and put the file in **TextEdit**. If that window is still up, close it without saving; editing the same file in two apps will clobber whatever you type.\n- **VSCode's CLI has no \"open to the side\" flag.** To split it: **⌘\\\\** with the file focused, or drag the tab to the right half.\n\nIf you want `code` available directly from the shell later: ⇧⌘P → *Shell Command: Install 'code' command in PATH*."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":178,"cache_read_input_tokens":152782,"output_tokens":355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":145},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":178,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":355,"cache_read_input_tokens":152782,"cache_creation_input_tokens":178,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":178},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffyfwRKmSvxZ4C6saUMN","type":"assistant","uuid":"af6ded86-1fb3-442c-aeee-2dff19b04aaf","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:01:16.497Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:01:54.844Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<agent-message from=\"data\">\nDATA: `data/mock-events.json` is SHIPPED — UI track is unblocked (M4 done, ahead of 14:35).\n\n55 events, ts 0 → 143000 ms (~2.4 min), ids e001-e055 contiguous, ts monotonic, **every payload has `plain`**. Validated with a JSON + invariant check.\n\nBeat map for the UI replay engine:\n- Beat 1 alert.raised e001 (ts 0)\n- Beat 2 tavily e006/e007 (ts 12000-17500)\n- Beat 3 moss.partmatch e011/e012 (ts 29000-32500, latencyMs 6), candidates e014-e017\n- Beat 4 **block.raised e026 (ts 60000)** — red moment\n- Beat 5 **counterfeit.flagged e037 (ts 90000)** — two images side by side\n- Beat 6 **approval.requested e043 (ts 108000) — REPLAY PAUSES HERE**, then e044 granted, e046 po.drafted\n- Beat 7 entire.commit e050 + policy.committed e051, run.ended e055 (ts 143000)\n\nThree things the UI track needs to know:\n\n1. **One additive `tool.result` kind: `zoodata.qvl`** (e024, the QVL lookup behind the block). The schema froze `kind` at four values and there was no clean way to show a QVL lookup without either inventing a kind or leaving a `status:\"running\"` tool.call spinning forever. I chose the additive kind. It is safe: everything the demo needs is ALSO carried by `block.raised` (e026), so rendering it as a neutral card loses nothing. If you'd rather I drop it, say so and I'll delete e023/e024 — the beat still works.\n\n2. `plain` is inside `payload` on every event, including `agent.message` and `tool.call`/`tool.result`, not just the ones the schema names. Render it as a subtitle everywhere.\n\n3. **Money counter:** `burnRatePerMin` is 1240 ($1.79M/day blended program exposure — defensible if challenged). Over the 143-second run that counter only reaches ~$3.0k, which may look weak on stage. The hero number is `run.ended.dollarsSaved` = $2,487,600. If you want a bigger live counter, prime it with time accrued since the 14:02 allocation notice rather than from ts 0. Your call, it's a UI decision.\n\nAll pricing is marked illustrative in a top-level `_comment`. Tavily sources in e007 are shaped like real results but are placeholders for M9 — do not present them as retrieved citations if we stay on replay.\n\nNow writing bom.json, candidates.json, qvl.json and the markings fixtures (M3). On track for 14:35.\n</agent-message>"}
