{"parentUuid":"4c6ab539-22e4-4040-ae18-700b1a9efc42","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffyjFGwckZPieyuS7Zf3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"DATA shipped the mock event log early — UI is unblocked. Three decisions came with it; making them now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1489,"cache_read_input_tokens":152960,"output_tokens":3173,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1224},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1489,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3173,"cache_read_input_tokens":152960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1489},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffyjEqQuA43UPyJtRcYJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"d7a32fcb-e0a0-4bca-9553-f0acc6b7f690","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:02:13.942Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"d7a32fcb-e0a0-4bca-9553-f0acc6b7f690","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffyjFGwckZPieyuS7Zf3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QU8ZcdDeDo1U6Dh366jmWV","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"data","summary":"Rename zoodata.qvl to qvl.lookup","message":"Keep the additive tool.result kind but rename it from `zoodata.qvl` to `qvl.lookup` — calling a local JSON lookup \"ZooData\" is a credibility risk we don't need.\n\nYour reasoning for adding it was right and the call was good: a tool.call left spinning forever is worse, and unknown kinds render as neutral cards so nothing breaks. Keep e023/e024.\n\nThe one problem is the name. ZooData is ZooWork's URL-to-structured-JSON product. If the QVL lookup is actually reading data/qvl.json off disk, labelling the result `zoodata.*` claims a sponsor integration we aren't making. We are chasing the Best Use of ZooWork prize, so a judge may well probe exactly that, and \"well, no, that one's a local file\" in front of the room costs more than the kind name is worth. Our whole thesis is provenance — we don't get to be loose about our own.\n\nSo: `kind: \"qvl.lookup\"`. Leave `tool: \"zoodata\"` on the tool.call if and only if AGENTS ends up genuinely routing that lookup through ZooData at M8; otherwise set the tool field to something accurate for a local lookup. I've told AGENTS this is their call to make.\n\nEverything else in your report is approved as-is: `plain` inside every payload is an improvement over the schema's minimum, and I've told UI to render it as a subtitle everywhere.\n\nOn the money counter — I'm taking your suggestion to prime it from the 14:02 allocation notice rather than ts 0, with the label stating that explicitly. Nothing further needed from you there, it's a UI change.\n\nCarry on with bom/candidates/qvl/markings for M3.","type":"message","recipient":"data","content":"Keep the additive tool.result kind but rename it …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1489,"cache_read_input_tokens":152960,"output_tokens":3173,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1224},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1489,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3173,"cache_read_input_tokens":152960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1489},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QU8ZcdDeDo1U6Dh366jmWV":{"to":"data","summary":"Rename zoodata.qvl to qvl.lookup","message":"Keep the additive tool.result kind but rename it from `zoodata.qvl` to `qvl.lookup` — calling a local JSON lookup \"ZooData\" is a credibility risk we don't need.\n\nYour reasoning for adding it was right and the call was good: a tool.call left spinning forever is worse, and unknown kinds render as neutral cards so nothing breaks. Keep e023/e024.\n\nThe one problem is the name. ZooData is ZooWork's URL-to-structured-JSON product. If the QVL lookup is actually reading data/qvl.json off disk, labelling the result `zoodata.*` claims a sponsor integration we aren't making. We are chasing the Best Use of ZooWork prize, so a judge may well probe exactly that, and \"well, no, that one's a local file\" in front of the room costs more than the kind name is worth. Our whole thesis is provenance — we don't get to be loose about our own.\n\nSo: `kind: \"qvl.lookup\"`. Leave `tool: \"zoodata\"` on the tool.call if and only if AGENTS ends up genuinely routing that lookup through ZooData at M8; otherwise set the tool field to something accurate for a local lookup. I've told AGENTS this is their call to make.\n\nEverything else in your report is approved as-is: `plain` inside every payload is an improvement over the schema's minimum, and I've told UI to render it as a subtitle everywhere.\n\nOn the money counter — I'm taking your suggestion to prime it from the 14:02 allocation notice rather than ts 0, with the label stating that explicitly. Nothing further needed from you there, it's a UI change.\n\nCarry on with bom/candidates/qvl/markings for M3."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffyjEqQuA43UPyJtRcYJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2caae63-b186-4786-8abe-e74c1b8ee8ca","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:02:23.066Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"a2caae63-b186-4786-8abe-e74c1b8ee8ca","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"165e70d9-e450-49f9-a2b7-12dba7111ca3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QU8ZcdDeDo1U6Dh366jmWV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Message queued for delivery to data at its next tool round.\",\"pin\":{\"id\":\"afaa00984109ea35d\",\"name\":\"data\",\"ref\":\"66fa47\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"70715247-3823-4adc-8e39-3d990d7e09c1","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:02:23.121Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Message queued for delivery to data at its next tool round.","pin":{"id":"afaa00984109ea35d","name":"data","ref":"66fa47"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2caae63-b186-4786-8abe-e74c1b8ee8ca","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"70715247-3823-4adc-8e39-3d990d7e09c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffyjFGwckZPieyuS7Zf3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wd92AS62HpYJvWCe772hcR","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ui","summary":"Mock events shipped; three UI decisions","message":"data/mock-events.json is SHIPPED and validated — swap off your stub now. 55 events, e001-e055, ts 0 to 143000ms.\n\nBeat map for your replay engine and keyboard skip (→ should jump between these):\n- Beat 1 alert.raised e001 (ts 0)\n- Beat 2 tavily e006/e007 (ts 12000-17500)\n- Beat 3 moss.partmatch e011/e012 (ts 29000-32500, latencyMs 6) + candidates e014-e017\n- Beat 4 block.raised e026 (ts 60000) — the red moment\n- Beat 5 counterfeit.flagged e037 (ts 90000) — two images side by side\n- Beat 6 approval.requested e043 (ts 108000) — REPLAY PAUSES, then e044 granted, e046 po.drafted\n- Beat 7 entire.commit e050 + policy.committed e051, run.ended e055 (ts 143000)\n\nThree decisions, all yours to implement:\n\n1. There is one additive tool.result kind beyond the four in the frozen schema, for the QVL lookup behind the block (e023/e024). It is being renamed `zoodata.qvl` → `qvl.lookup`; render it as a labelled evidence card. Everything that beat needs is also carried by block.raised (e026), so if it gives you any trouble, render it neutral and move on.\n\n2. `plain` is present inside `payload` on EVERY event, not just the ones the schema names — including agent.message and tool.call/tool.result. Render it as a subtitle everywhere. This is the single highest-leverage thing for the Design score, because it is what keeps a judge who doesn't know what a QVL is following all seven beats.\n\n3. Money counter: prime it from the 14:02 allocation notice, not from ts 0. At burnRatePerMin 1240 the counter only reaches ~$3.0k across the 143-second run, which reads as trivial on stage and undercuts the tension. Priming from the notice time is honest as long as the label says so — render it as \"Exposure accrued since 14:02 allocation notice\" or similar, with the start time visible. Do not invent a rate; 1240/min is the defensible number ($1.79M/day blended program exposure).\n\nRelated: the hero number is run.ended.dollarsSaved = $2,487,600. Give that its own large, deliberate treatment at the end of the run — the climbing counter is tension, but THAT is the number the judges should remember. It is the whole P&L argument in one figure.\n\nOne honesty constraint: the Tavily sources in e007 are placeholder-shaped, not retrieved. If we are still on replay at demo time, do not style them to look like live retrieved citations. A neutral \"source\" treatment is fine; a fake live-fetch animation is not.","type":"message","recipient":"ui","content":"data/mock-events.json is SHIPPED and validated — …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1489,"cache_read_input_tokens":152960,"output_tokens":3173,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1224},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1489,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3173,"cache_read_input_tokens":152960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1489},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Wd92AS62HpYJvWCe772hcR":{"to":"ui","summary":"Mock events shipped; three UI decisions","message":"data/mock-events.json is SHIPPED and validated — swap off your stub now. 55 events, e001-e055, ts 0 to 143000ms.\n\nBeat map for your replay engine and keyboard skip (→ should jump between these):\n- Beat 1 alert.raised e001 (ts 0)\n- Beat 2 tavily e006/e007 (ts 12000-17500)\n- Beat 3 moss.partmatch e011/e012 (ts 29000-32500, latencyMs 6) + candidates e014-e017\n- Beat 4 block.raised e026 (ts 60000) — the red moment\n- Beat 5 counterfeit.flagged e037 (ts 90000) — two images side by side\n- Beat 6 approval.requested e043 (ts 108000) — REPLAY PAUSES, then e044 granted, e046 po.drafted\n- Beat 7 entire.commit e050 + policy.committed e051, run.ended e055 (ts 143000)\n\nThree decisions, all yours to implement:\n\n1. There is one additive tool.result kind beyond the four in the frozen schema, for the QVL lookup behind the block (e023/e024). It is being renamed `zoodata.qvl` → `qvl.lookup`; render it as a labelled evidence card. Everything that beat needs is also carried by block.raised (e026), so if it gives you any trouble, render it neutral and move on.\n\n2. `plain` is present inside `payload` on EVERY event, not just the ones the schema names — including agent.message and tool.call/tool.result. Render it as a subtitle everywhere. This is the single highest-leverage thing for the Design score, because it is what keeps a judge who doesn't know what a QVL is following all seven beats.\n\n3. Money counter: prime it from the 14:02 allocation notice, not from ts 0. At burnRatePerMin 1240 the counter only reaches ~$3.0k across the 143-second run, which reads as trivial on stage and undercuts the tension. Priming from the notice time is honest as long as the label says so — render it as \"Exposure accrued since 14:02 allocation notice\" or similar, with the start time visible. Do not invent a rate; 1240/min is the defensible number ($1.79M/day blended program exposure).\n\nRelated: the hero number is run.ended.dollarsSaved = $2,487,600. Give that its own large, deliberate treatment at the end of the run — the climbing counter is tension, but THAT is the number the judges should remember. It is the whole P&L argument in one figure.\n\nOne honesty constraint: the Tavily sources in e007 are placeholder-shaped, not retrieved. If we are still on replay at demo time, do not style them to look like live retrieved citations. A neutral \"source\" treatment is fine; a fake live-fetch animation is not."}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CffyjEqQuA43UPyJtRcYJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5cc15b1-2e30-438b-a2cc-b58b70b03bee","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:02:35.172Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
