{"parentUuid":"bfbecfef-6f6f-427a-8e40-a9f1bbd820c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffyo8PKP8c7CPDNaWQrH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**M4 shipped at 14:28, ahead of schedule** — 55 events, a 2.4-minute run, UI track unblocked and off its stub.\n\nThree calls I made on your behalf:\n\n- **Renamed a tool result `zoodata.qvl` → `qvl.lookup`.** It was going to label a local JSON file read as ZooData. With a Best Use of ZooWork prize in play, a judge may probe exactly that, and \"well, no, that one's a local file\" in front of the room costs more than a name is worth. The project's whole thesis is provenance — we don't get to be loose about our own.\n- **Money counter now primes from the 14:02 allocation notice**, labelled with that start time. At $1,240/min it only reached ~$3.0k across a 143-second run, which reads as trivial on stage. The hero number is the close: **$2,487,600 saved** — that's the one judges should walk away with.\n- **Tavily sources in the mock log stay neutrally styled.** They're placeholder-shaped, not retrieved. If we demo on replay, they must not be dressed up as live citations.\n\nCurrent state: `plain` subtitles land on every single event, which is the highest-leverage thing available for the Design score — a judge who doesn't know what a QVL is can still follow all seven beats.\n\n**Still on you:** the keys in [.env](.env), and photographing a real DIMM. That photo is now more important than it was — beat 5 feeds it to a ZooWork vision model through a custom-tool image block, so the pixels genuinely drive the demo. Shoot one clean module and one with an altered label.\n\nWant the 3-minute presentation script drafted now? The beat timings are pinned to real timestamps, so I can write narration that lands against the actual replay."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":681,"cache_read_input_tokens":157919,"output_tokens":573,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":681,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":157919,"cache_creation_input_tokens":681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":681},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cffyo82k8HprwD5hAtsv8","type":"assistant","uuid":"1cf4271f-9662-4d09-8079-0a37486d7ea6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:02:57.645Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
