{"parentUuid":"22faccb1-4cf6-40cb-88dc-eab6211c2eae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffypbgv7kguWHApBCU6E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Useful — Entire's primitive is a **trail**, and trails have URLs. That makes beat 7 fully real instead of mocked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3048,"cache_read_input_tokens":158600,"output_tokens":1952,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":671},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3048,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1952,"cache_read_input_tokens":158600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3048},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffypbJrKwS8szJEAKdwt","type":"assistant","uuid":"cbd2e9ac-28f9-4f5c-b7ef-93d74ec4ec7e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:03:20.281Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"cbd2e9ac-28f9-4f5c-b7ef-93d74ec4ec7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffypbgv7kguWHApBCU6E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FCM1brCyCEbVcJ3k7ujG2F","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"agents","summary":"Use entire trails; get real trail URL","message":"Entire is free and needs no key — and its primitive is a \"trail\", not just a session-attached commit. Make beat 7 real rather than mocked.\n\nFrom their slide: `entire trail resume [trail-id]` — \"Branch, checkpoints, and session context already attached.\" It works across Claude Code and Codex, and trails have shareable URLs (\"Or paste the trail URL: Work on this trail: [URL]\").\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n1. Drop ENTIRE_TOKEN from your env expectations. Install the CLI (`curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash`) and use it directly. If it wants an interactive `entire login`, flag it in status/agents.md and I'll have the user run it — do not block on it.\n\n2. **Beat 7 should produce a REAL trail URL.** You are a Claude Code session, and Entire captures Claude Code sessions. So when you make the QVL/approved-alternates change to data/qvl.json, do it under Entire so the trail genuinely contains the agent session that made the sourcing decision. Then put that real URL into `policy.committed.blameUrl` per docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md.\n\nThat turns the closing beat from a claim into a demonstration: the presenter clicks the link on stage and a judge sees the actual prompts and tool calls behind the QVL change. \"Git tells you what changed, Entire tells you why\" stops being a slogan we quote and becomes a thing we do. For an audit-traceability pitch — which is our entire framing for why procurement needs this — that is the difference between the argument landing and not.\n\nIf the real trail URL doesn't materialise by the 16:30 freeze, fall back to the mocked hash and say nothing on stage about clicking through. Do not fake a URL that 404s in front of judges; that is a worse outcome than not having one.\n\nKeep this inside your existing scope — no new milestones, it replaces the adapter work you already have at M10.","type":"message","recipient":"agents","content":"Entire is free and needs no key — and its primiti…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3048,"cache_read_input_tokens":158600,"output_tokens":1952,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":671},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3048,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1952,"cache_read_input_tokens":158600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3048,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3048},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FCM1brCyCEbVcJ3k7ujG2F":{"to":"agents","summary":"Use entire trails; get real trail URL","message":"Entire is free and needs no key — and its primitive is a \"trail\", not just a session-attached commit. Make beat 7 real rather than mocked.\n\nFrom their slide: `entire trail resume [trail-id]` — \"Branch, checkpoints, and session context already attached.\" It works across Claude Code and Codex, and trails have shareable URLs (\"Or paste the trail URL: Work on this trail: [URL]\").\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n1. Drop ENTIRE_TOKEN from your env expectations. Install the CLI (`curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash`) and use it directly. If it wants an interactive `entire login`, flag it in status/agents.md and I'll have the user run it — do not block on it.\n\n2. **Beat 7 should produce a REAL trail URL.** You are a Claude Code session, and Entire captures Claude Code sessions. So when you make the QVL/approved-alternates change to data/qvl.json, do it under Entire so the trail genuinely contains the agent session that made the sourcing decision. Then put that real URL into `policy.committed.blameUrl` per docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md.\n\nThat turns the closing beat from a claim into a demonstration: the presenter clicks the link on stage and a judge sees the actual prompts and tool calls behind the QVL change. \"Git tells you what changed, Entire tells you why\" stops being a slogan we quote and becomes a thing we do. For an audit-traceability pitch — which is our entire framing for why procurement needs this — that is the difference between the argument landing and not.\n\nIf the real trail URL doesn't materialise by the 16:30 freeze, fall back to the mocked hash and say nothing on stage about clicking through. Do not fake a URL that 404s in front of judges; that is a worse outcome than not having one.\n\nKeep this inside your existing scope — no new milestones, it replaces the adapter work you already have at M10."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffypbJrKwS8szJEAKdwt","type":"assistant","uuid":"caa575d2-1a2c-43d4-8ce4-420ef19b073e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:03:30.817Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
