{"parentUuid":"7962bd9d-272d-4b77-b2a8-708bee4616b9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cca4108e-01cd-4bb1-8a95-def08ab6de13","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019ffZF4jhtPjmHZu9kZ16yr","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/.env.example has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"fc544dbb-bb3a-40c6-b0a4-b4a481a76228","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:03:43.353Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/.env.example","oldString":"# --- Entire (git network / session provenance) ---\n# Likely authenticates via `entire login` rather than an env var.\n# Check status/recon.md before setting this.\nENTIRE_TOKEN=","newString":"# --- Entire (git network / session provenance) ---\n# NO KEY NEEDED — Entire is free. Just install the CLI:\n#   curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash\n# Its primitive is a \"trail\" (entire trail resume [trail-id]); trails have shareable URLs.","originalFile":"# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit it.\n#   cp .env.example .env\n\n# --- ZooWork (Best Use of ZooWork prize) ---\n# VERIFIED against the shipped SDK (@zoowork-ai/sdk 0.10.2, dist/).\n# Exactly ONE variable is required:\nZOOWORK_API_KEY=\n\n# Do NOT set these:\n#   ZOOWORK_BASE_URL     leave UNSET. The default already includes the /service/v1\n#                        prefix; setting it wrong 404s every call.\n#   ZOOWORK_ORG_ID       does not exist. The gateway derives the tenant from the key.\n#   ZOOWORK_AGENT_ID     not an SDK input. Agent IDs come back from createAgent()\n#                        at runtime and we persist them ourselves.\n#   ZOOWORK_WEBHOOK_SECRET   only for verifying inbound signed webhooks. We receive none.\n\n# --- Moss (on-device semantic search) ---\nMOSS_PROJECT_ID=\nMOSS_PROJECT_KEY=\n# Hackathon code: GALLERYHACKS\n\n# --- Tavily (web research) ---\nTAVILY_API_KEY=\n\n# --- BAND (multi-agent rooms) ---\nBAND_API_KEY=\n\n# --- Entire (git network / session provenance) ---\n# Likely authenticates via `entire login` rather than an env var.\n# Check status/recon.md before setting this.\nENTIRE_TOKEN=\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":6,"newStart":26,"newLines":6,"lines":[" BAND_API_KEY="," "," # --- Entire (git network / session provenance) ---","-# Likely authenticates via `entire login` rather than an env var.","-# Check status/recon.md before setting this.","-ENTIRE_TOKEN=","+# NO KEY NEEDED — Entire is free. Just install the CLI:","+#   curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash","+# Its primitive is a \"trail\" (entire trail resume [trail-id]); trails have shareable URLs."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7962bd9d-272d-4b77-b2a8-708bee4616b9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"fc544dbb-bb3a-40c6-b0a4-b4a481a76228","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14994970 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c22a6c4f-a575-41c8-b673-c1908af12d52","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:03:43.381Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14994970 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"c22a6c4f-a575-41c8-b673-c1908af12d52","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffysEdyNugusVCXqDRcf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Skip `ENTIRE_TOKEN` in your [.env](.env)** — it's a leftover from the earlier template. No key needed. Just:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash\n```\n\nSo your key list is down to four: ZooWork, Moss (×2), Tavily, BAND.\n\n**Why the trail primitive matters more than it looks:** trails carry branch, checkpoints and session context, they work across Claude Code, and they have shareable URLs. Your build agents *are* Claude Code sessions — so when the QVL change gets made under Entire, the trail genuinely contains the agent session that made the sourcing decision.\n\nThat upgrades beat 7 from a claim to a demonstration. The presenter clicks a real link on stage and a judge sees the actual prompts and tool calls behind the QVL change. *\"Git tells you what changed, Entire tells you why\"* stops being a slogan you quote and becomes a thing you do — which is the difference between your audit-traceability framing landing and sounding like a pitch.\n\nI've told AGENTS to fall back to the mocked hash if the real URL doesn't land by the 16:30 freeze, and to say nothing about clicking through in that case. A URL that 404s in front of judges is worse than no URL.\n\n**14:42. ~2h15m to submission.** Next due: RECON notes, MOSS text-match code, and UI rendering a full run by 15:15."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":478,"cache_read_input_tokens":163809,"output_tokens":475,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":478,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":475,"cache_read_input_tokens":163809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":478,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":478},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffysEH9MSPaH3dn7NJUo","type":"assistant","uuid":"892f321d-67f4-4f14-ba6c-13ddb84b21f7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:03:50.470Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:03:58.388Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae1341cad99a02d12</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_011AohVHJ8Z7nBfvHu2o4PWn</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/ae1341cad99a02d12.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Sponsor SDK integration recon\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>M2 delivered at 14:18, seven minutes ahead of the gate. AGENTS was unblocked at 14:05.\n\n**Method:** cloned the ZooWork and BAND SDK repos and read the actual source rather than fetching doc pages, so those two are source-reviewed rather than recalled. Tavily and Entire went to parallel subagents against live official docs.\n\n**Four findings that change build decisions:**\n\n1. **ZooWork model IDs do need provider prefixes** — `litellm/gpt-5.6-terra`. Don't hardcode; select from `listModels()` filtering `selectable !== false &amp;&amp; default_for?.includes('model')` or you get `409 model_not_selectable`.\n\n2. **BAND has real rooms but no native Critic/veto.** The entire event vocabulary is five strings (`tool_call`, `tool_result`, `thought`, `error`, `task`) — no block, no veto, no gate, no advance-turn call. A \"Critic that blocks\" is prompt-and-convention; nothing halts the room. I sent this to AGENTS at 14:05 and confirmed their local orchestrator is the right call. Note the org is `band-ai`, not `Band-AI/band`.\n\n3. **The real block gate is ZooWork `custom_tools`** — the run genuinely pauses until the backend calls `resolveCustomToolCall`. Runtime-enforced rather than social, and it strengthens the one submission with a named prize. Recommended for beat 4.\n\n4. **Beat 7's command is `entire why`, not `entire blame`.** `blame` gives a per-line attribution table; `why` prints the actual prompt text, which is what the auditor beat needs.\n\n**Two traps that would each cost an hour.** `entire enable -y --agent claude-code` must run *before* the agent session starts — it's a git-hook install, not a `run` wrapper, and missing it leaves no session to attach with no recovery. Worth doing in the repo now. And ZooWork cannot attach a local/stdio or authenticated MCP server (remote HTTP only; the `credential` slug is accepted but no endpoint exists to store the secret), so if anyone planned to reach Moss over MCP, that won't work — call Moss from our own backend and feed it in via a `custom_tools` resolution.\n\n**Flagged honestly as UNVERIFIED:** the Entire hosted shareable blame URL is the biggest per-sponsor demo risk. No evidence of a public no-login share link or `--share` flag, and the browser view provably needs an account plus a connected, pushed repo. A URL pattern surfaced only via search-engine synthesis, never a primary doc — it shouldn't be typed on stage. The terminal path is verified end-to-end, which matches cut-ladder item 5. Smaller gaps (Tavily extract timeout default, `--agent` value spellings) are listed in `status/recon.md` with the ten-second commands that settle them.\n\nTavily is comfortably free for the demo: 1,000 credits/month, 1 per basic search. Avoid `/research` at 15–250 credits per request.\n\nFiles: `docs/INTEGRATION.md` and `status/recon.md` only — no cross-track edits; repos cloned read-only into the scratchpad.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>123724</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>21</tool_uses><duration_ms>628405</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
