{"parentUuid":"51088271-8ead-4115-b949-965cb8bd692a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cffz1eE2DjnsUeSPHbp4g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LS9zeGgUengw4rrt4hGBKq","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"agents","summary":"Beat 7 is terminal entire why, not a URL","message":"Correcting my earlier instruction on beat 7: demo it in the TERMINAL with `entire why`, not by clicking a shareable URL on stage.\n\nI told you to get a real trail URL into policy.committed.blameUrl and have the presenter click it. RECON has since flagged that hosted share link as the single biggest per-sponsor demo risk: no evidence of a public no-login share link or a --share flag, the browser view provably requires an account plus a connected and pushed repo, and the one URL pattern that surfaced came from search-engine synthesis rather than any primary doc. It must not be typed on stage.\n\nThe terminal path is verified end to end, so that is the demo. Two specifics from RECON:\n- The command is **`entire why`**, not `entire blame`. `blame` returns a per-line attribution table; `why` prints the actual prompt text, which is the thing that makes the auditor beat land.\n- `entire enable -y --agent claude-code` must run **before** an agent session starts. It installs a git hook rather than wrapping `run`, so missing it leaves no session to attach and there is no recovery after the fact. I am installing the CLI and running enable in the repo now, so you should find it already in place — verify rather than assume, and tell me in status/agents.md if it isn't.\n\nKeep `blameUrl` in the event payload as a field; just populate it with the trail reference and let the UI render it as text rather than as a live link. If a genuinely working no-login URL turns up before the 16:30 freeze, we can upgrade — but the plan of record is the terminal.\n\nHonestly this is the better demo anyway. Running a command live in front of judges and having the original prompt print out is more convincing than a click-through, and it cannot 404.\n\nTwo other RECON findings in case they haven't reached you: ZooWork model IDs need provider prefixes (`litellm/gpt-5.6-terra`) and should be selected from `listModels()` filtering `selectable !== false && default_for?.includes('model')`, or you get 409 model_not_selectable. And use ZooWork `custom_tools` as the gate for beat 4's block — the run genuinely pauses until the backend calls `resolveCustomToolCall`, which makes Engineering's veto runtime-enforced rather than prompt convention. That is a real strengthening of the one submission with a named prize, and worth prioritising over the Market agent.","type":"message","recipient":"agents","content":"Correcting my earlier instruction on beat 7: demo…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":508,"cache_read_input_tokens":169793,"output_tokens":2200,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":117},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":508,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2200,"cache_read_input_tokens":169793,"cache_creation_input_tokens":508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":508},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LS9zeGgUengw4rrt4hGBKq":{"to":"agents","summary":"Beat 7 is terminal entire why, not a URL","message":"Correcting my earlier instruction on beat 7: demo it in the TERMINAL with `entire why`, not by clicking a shareable URL on stage.\n\nI told you to get a real trail URL into policy.committed.blameUrl and have the presenter click it. RECON has since flagged that hosted share link as the single biggest per-sponsor demo risk: no evidence of a public no-login share link or a --share flag, the browser view provably requires an account plus a connected and pushed repo, and the one URL pattern that surfaced came from search-engine synthesis rather than any primary doc. It must not be typed on stage.\n\nThe terminal path is verified end to end, so that is the demo. Two specifics from RECON:\n- The command is **`entire why`**, not `entire blame`. `blame` returns a per-line attribution table; `why` prints the actual prompt text, which is the thing that makes the auditor beat land.\n- `entire enable -y --agent claude-code` must run **before** an agent session starts. It installs a git hook rather than wrapping `run`, so missing it leaves no session to attach and there is no recovery after the fact. I am installing the CLI and running enable in the repo now, so you should find it already in place — verify rather than assume, and tell me in status/agents.md if it isn't.\n\nKeep `blameUrl` in the event payload as a field; just populate it with the trail reference and let the UI render it as text rather than as a live link. If a genuinely working no-login URL turns up before the 16:30 freeze, we can upgrade — but the plan of record is the terminal.\n\nHonestly this is the better demo anyway. Running a command live in front of judges and having the original prompt print out is more convincing than a click-through, and it cannot 404.\n\nTwo other RECON findings in case they haven't reached you: ZooWork model IDs need provider prefixes (`litellm/gpt-5.6-terra`) and should be selected from `listModels()` filtering `selectable !== false && default_for?.includes('model')`, or you get 409 model_not_selectable. And use ZooWork `custom_tools` as the gate for beat 4's block — the run genuinely pauses until the backend calls `resolveCustomToolCall`, which makes Engineering's veto runtime-enforced rather than prompt convention. That is a real strengthening of the one submission with a named prize, and worth prioritising over the Market agent."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cffz1dUNnELYHp8W7GXnw","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f79566a-8427-4ffb-bd90-96dfc7c31355","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:05:52.882Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
