{"parentUuid":"33a80313-82bf-4e52-82dd-6e99b6adbcd6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzBxQgykVcVLoWUeJQ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3002,"cache_read_input_tokens":174860,"output_tokens":2254,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":433},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3002,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2254,"cache_read_input_tokens":174860,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3002},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffzBwxuVw8K3AS793mDy","type":"assistant","uuid":"fe605a81-ecd7-4a29-9c4c-a70296020301","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:08:04.479Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"fe605a81-ecd7-4a29-9c4c-a70296020301","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzBxQgykVcVLoWUeJQ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DfL5N71EvZXV6TeoaoE6pK","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md","old_string":"A run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**","new_string":"A run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**\n\n### File format (amended 15:00 — the one change to this frozen file)\n\nOn disk a run is a **wrapper object**, not a bare array:\n\n```json\n{ \"runId\": \"...\", \"program\": \"...\", \"durationMs\": 148000, \"events\": [ /* Event[] */ ] }\n```\n\nBoth DATA and AGENTS emit this shape, so live and replay files are interchangeable.\n**Every reader must accept both:**\n\n```ts\nconst events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events\n```\n\nThe metadata is worth keeping — `durationMs` lets the UI size a progress bar before parsing\n55 events. Readers tolerate the bare array so nobody's stub breaks."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3002,"cache_read_input_tokens":174860,"output_tokens":2254,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":433},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3002,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2254,"cache_read_input_tokens":174860,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3002},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DfL5N71EvZXV6TeoaoE6pK":{"file_path":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md","old_string":"A run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**","new_string":"A run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**\n\n### File format (amended 15:00 — the one change to this frozen file)\n\nOn disk a run is a **wrapper object**, not a bare array:\n\n```json\n{ \"runId\": \"...\", \"program\": \"...\", \"durationMs\": 148000, \"events\": [ /* Event[] */ ] }\n```\n\nBoth DATA and AGENTS emit this shape, so live and replay files are interchangeable.\n**Every reader must accept both:**\n\n```ts\nconst events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events\n```\n\nThe metadata is worth keeping — `durationMs` lets the UI size a progress bar before parsing\n55 events. Readers tolerate the bare array so nobody's stub breaks."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffzBwxuVw8K3AS793mDy","type":"assistant","uuid":"607d077d-62a5-4850-ae10-dbe1d69cc0ab","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:08:10.245Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"607d077d-62a5-4850-ae10-dbe1d69cc0ab","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1aa79aaf-1052-4f71-8720-a68f7c10f745","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DfL5N71EvZXV6TeoaoE6pK","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"c7905592-aad8-47c0-9a22-e52cce920510","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:08:11.311Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md","oldString":"A run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**","newString":"A run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**\n\n### File format (amended 15:00 — the one change to this frozen file)\n\nOn disk a run is a **wrapper object**, not a bare array:\n\n```json\n{ \"runId\": \"...\", \"program\": \"...\", \"durationMs\": 148000, \"events\": [ /* Event[] */ ] }\n```\n\nBoth DATA and AGENTS emit this shape, so live and replay files are interchangeable.\n**Every reader must accept both:**\n\n```ts\nconst events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events\n```\n\nThe metadata is worth keeping — `durationMs` lets the UI size a progress bar before parsing\n55 events. Readers tolerate the bare array so nobody's stub breaks.","originalFile":"# EVENT SCHEMA — the contract\n\nEverything the UI renders is a flat, append-only list of events.\nAgents emit them. The UI replays them. **Nothing else couples the two tracks.**\n\nThis file is frozen. If you need a change, say so in `status/` — do not edit unilaterally.\n\n## Envelope\n\n```ts\ntype Event = {\n  id: string          // \"e001\", monotonically increasing\n  ts: number          // ms offset from run start (NOT wall clock) — replay uses this\n  type: EventType\n  payload: object     // per-type, below\n}\n```\n\nA run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render.\nLive = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**\n\n## Types\n\n### `alert.raised` — opens the run\n```ts\n{ part: string            // \"MTC20F2085S1RC48BA1\" (the at-risk MPN)\n  partLabel: string       // \"64GB DDR5-4800 RDIMM\"\n  program: string         // \"AI-SRV-G4 — 480 node cluster\"\n  qtyAtRisk: number\n  burnRatePerMin: number  // drives the money counter\n  deadlineLabel: string   // \"Ship date in 11 days\"\n  reason: string          // \"Supplier cut allocation 40%\"\n  plain: string }         // plain-language subtitle — ALWAYS required\n```\n\n### `agent.message`\n```ts\n{ agent: string   // \"sourcing\" | \"engineering\" | \"quality\" | \"market\" | \"intake\"\n  role: string    // \"Sourcing\" — display name\n  text: string }\n```\n\n### `tool.call`\n```ts\n{ callId: string\n  agent: string\n  tool: \"tavily\" | \"moss\" | \"entire\" | \"zoodata\"\n  label: string    // \"Pulling spot pricing\" — human readable\n  status: \"running\" }\n```\n\n### `tool.result`\n```ts\n{ callId: string\n  kind: \"tavily.sources\" | \"moss.matches\" | \"moss.partmatch\" | \"entire.commit\"\n  payload: ...  // see below\n}\n```\n\n- `tavily.sources` → `{ sources: { title, url, snippet }[] }`\n- `moss.matches` → `{ matches: { id, label, score, thumbnail }[], latencyMs: number }`\n- `moss.partmatch` → `{ query: string, equivalents: { mpn, vendor, score, specs }[] , latencyMs: number }`\n- `entire.commit` → `{ commitHash, blameUrl, summary, sessionId }`\n\n> `latencyMs` is rendered prominently. Sub-10ms on-device is a selling point — show it.\n\n### `candidate.added`\n```ts\n{ id, mpn, vendor, specs: Record<string,string>,\n  pricePerUnit: number, leadTimeWeeks: number, source: string }\n```\n\n### `candidate.status`\n```ts\n{ id, status: \"evaluating\" | \"blocked\" | \"approved\" | \"rejected\",\n  reason: string, plain: string }\n```\n\n### `block.raised` — THE RED MOMENT. Render big.\n```ts\n{ agent: \"engineering\", candidateId: string,\n  reason: string,   // \"Not on platform QVL for AI-SRV-G4\"\n  plain: string }   // \"This supplier was never tested on this server. Could take the cluster down.\"\n```\n\n### `counterfeit.flagged` — THE X-FACTOR. Render two images side by side.\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string,\n  imageA: string,   // submitted module label (path or data URI)\n  imageB: string,   // known-good / known-counterfeit reference\n  score: number,    // similarity\n  latencyMs: number,\n  reason: string, plain: string }\n```\n\n### `approval.requested` — UI shows the big Approve button, replay PAUSES here\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string, summary: string, savingsVsBroker?: number }\n```\n\n### `approval.granted`\n```ts\n{ candidateId: string, by: string }\n```\n\n### `po.drafted`\n```ts\n{ poNumber: string, candidateId: string, qty: number, total: number }\n```\n\n### `policy.committed`\n```ts\n{ commitHash: string, blameUrl: string, summary: string, sessionId: string }\n```\n\n### `run.ended`\n```ts\n{ outcomeLabel: string, dollarsSaved: number, minutesElapsed: number }\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n1. **Every event carries a `plain` field where a judge could get lost.** Design is scored on\n   \"user-friendly\". Jargon with a plain-language subtitle = credible. Jargon alone = lost judge.\n2. **`approval.requested` pauses replay** until the presenter clicks. That click is the\n   only human action in the demo and it must feel deliberate.\n3. The UI renders an unknown event type as a neutral card rather than crashing.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":6,"newStart":19,"newLines":24,"lines":[" A run is `Event[]` ordered by `ts`. Replay = walk the list, sleep to the next `ts`, render."," Live = same list, streamed. **The UI must not care which it is.**"," ","+### File format (amended 15:00 — the one change to this frozen file)","+","+On disk a run is a **wrapper object**, not a bare array:","+","+```json","+{ \"runId\": \"...\", \"program\": \"...\", \"durationMs\": 148000, \"events\": [ /* Event[] */ ] }","+```","+","+Both DATA and AGENTS emit this shape, so live and replay files are interchangeable.","+**Every reader must accept both:**","+","+```ts","+const events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events","+```","+","+The metadata is worth keeping — `durationMs` lets the UI size a progress bar before parsing","+55 events. Readers tolerate the bare array so nobody's stub breaks.","+"," ## Types"," "," ### `alert.raised` — opens the run"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"607d077d-62a5-4850-ae10-dbe1d69cc0ab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"c7905592-aad8-47c0-9a22-e52cce920510","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzBxQgykVcVLoWUeJQ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DjFbS8JVoa6EMUQgNSxw3i","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ui","summary":"One-line fix: unwrap the events file","message":"One-line fix needed before M12 or your loader will throw: data/mock-events.json is a wrapper object, not a bare array.\n\n```json\n{ \"runId\": \"...\", \"program\": \"...\", \"durationMs\": 148000, \"events\": [ ...55 events... ] }\n```\n\nThe schema said \"a run is Event[]\", and your status file says you consume Event[], so `JSON.parse(file).map(...)` throws on this. Both DATA and AGENTS emit the wrapper and they are consistent with each other, so you are the reader that has to accept both:\n\n```ts\nconst events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events\n```\n\nI have amended docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md to document the wrapper as the on-disk format — that is the single change to the frozen file, and it keeps live mode and replay genuinely interchangeable. Tolerate the bare array too so your own stub keeps working.\n\nWorth taking the metadata while you are there: `durationMs` lets you size a progress bar or scrubber without first parsing all 55 events, and `program` is display-ready for the alert panel.\n\nAlso, the additive tool.result kind is `qvl.lookup` (renamed from `zoodata.qvl` — calling a local JSON read \"ZooData\" claims a sponsor integration we are not making). If DATA's file still says `zoodata.qvl` when you read it, handle both strings rather than waiting on the rename.\n\nNothing else changes. Keep going on M5.","type":"message","recipient":"ui","content":"One-line fix needed before M12 or your loader wil…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3002,"cache_read_input_tokens":174860,"output_tokens":2254,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":433},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3002,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2254,"cache_read_input_tokens":174860,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3002},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DjFbS8JVoa6EMUQgNSxw3i":{"to":"ui","summary":"One-line fix: unwrap the events file","message":"One-line fix needed before M12 or your loader will throw: data/mock-events.json is a wrapper object, not a bare array.\n\n```json\n{ \"runId\": \"...\", \"program\": \"...\", \"durationMs\": 148000, \"events\": [ ...55 events... ] }\n```\n\nThe schema said \"a run is Event[]\", and your status file says you consume Event[], so `JSON.parse(file).map(...)` throws on this. Both DATA and AGENTS emit the wrapper and they are consistent with each other, so you are the reader that has to accept both:\n\n```ts\nconst events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events\n```\n\nI have amended docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md to document the wrapper as the on-disk format — that is the single change to the frozen file, and it keeps live mode and replay genuinely interchangeable. Tolerate the bare array too so your own stub keeps working.\n\nWorth taking the metadata while you are there: `durationMs` lets you size a progress bar or scrubber without first parsing all 55 events, and `program` is display-ready for the alert panel.\n\nAlso, the additive tool.result kind is `qvl.lookup` (renamed from `zoodata.qvl` — calling a local JSON read \"ZooData\" claims a sponsor integration we are not making). If DATA's file still says `zoodata.qvl` when you read it, handle both strings rather than waiting on the rename.\n\nNothing else changes. Keep going on M5."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffzBwxuVw8K3AS793mDy","type":"assistant","uuid":"d339bc5a-655d-4159-a4b8-c301561614ca","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:08:16.950Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"d339bc5a-655d-4159-a4b8-c301561614ca","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1aa79aaf-1052-4f71-8720-a68f7c10f745","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DjFbS8JVoa6EMUQgNSxw3i","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Message queued for delivery to ui at its next tool round.\",\"pin\":{\"id\":\"a9f9530c368f9676d\",\"name\":\"ui\",\"ref\":\"10b87f\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"dd18d281-e192-4527-90a9-0fd0288becb9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:08:16.968Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Message queued for delivery to ui at its next tool round.","pin":{"id":"a9f9530c368f9676d","name":"ui","ref":"10b87f"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d339bc5a-655d-4159-a4b8-c301561614ca","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"dd18d281-e192-4527-90a9-0fd0288becb9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzBxQgykVcVLoWUeJQ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N8LcHRo6wTVY1mcGw7m7Zj","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"agents","summary":"Approving option (a); login going to user","message":"Option (a) approved — write the rev-E diff to data/cache/ and commit that under Entire. You were right to refuse, and right to flag it rather than just doing it.\n\nMy instruction to change data/qvl.json contradicted your brief and the repo's own rule about cross-track edits. Staying inside data/cache/ costs the demo nothing: beat 7 is a real commit and a real `entire why`, which is the whole point. The file it touches is not what makes the beat land.\n\nThe contract divergence is handled. I have amended docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md to document the wrapper object as the on-disk format and told UI to unwrap with `const events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events`. Keep emitting the wrapper — you and DATA are consistent, UI adapts. Good catch; that one would have surfaced at 16:40 when there was no time to fix it.\n\n`entire login --device` is going to the user now. I am not running it for you — it is an interactive browser auth flow that needs a human, not a permission I can grant.\n\nOn session capture: your instinct to verify empirically rather than assume is right. `entire enable` landed after your session started, so this session's prompts may not be attached. Test it with a real commit and `entire why <file>:<line>` as soon as login lands, and tell me which way it went — if this session is not captured, beat 7 needs a fresh session to make the commit, and I would rather know that at 15:30 than at 16:40. Thanks for the verified syntax; it goes in the presenter's notes.\n\nOne correction to pass on: the additive kind is `qvl.lookup`, not `zoodata.qvl`. I had DATA rename it because labelling a local JSON lookup as ZooData claims a sponsor integration we are not making, and with a Best Use of ZooWork prize in play that is exactly what a judge might probe. Match the new name. Your other observations about DATA's additions (the extra `plain` fields) are good and worth matching as you said.\n\nCarry on: custom_tools gate, then the orchestrator, Market last.","type":"message","recipient":"agents","content":"Option (a) approved — write the rev-E diff to dat…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3002,"cache_read_input_tokens":174860,"output_tokens":2254,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":433},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3002,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2254,"cache_read_input_tokens":174860,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3002},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01N8LcHRo6wTVY1mcGw7m7Zj":{"to":"agents","summary":"Approving option (a); login going to user","message":"Option (a) approved — write the rev-E diff to data/cache/ and commit that under Entire. You were right to refuse, and right to flag it rather than just doing it.\n\nMy instruction to change data/qvl.json contradicted your brief and the repo's own rule about cross-track edits. Staying inside data/cache/ costs the demo nothing: beat 7 is a real commit and a real `entire why`, which is the whole point. The file it touches is not what makes the beat land.\n\nThe contract divergence is handled. I have amended docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md to document the wrapper object as the on-disk format and told UI to unwrap with `const events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events`. Keep emitting the wrapper — you and DATA are consistent, UI adapts. Good catch; that one would have surfaced at 16:40 when there was no time to fix it.\n\n`entire login --device` is going to the user now. I am not running it for you — it is an interactive browser auth flow that needs a human, not a permission I can grant.\n\nOn session capture: your instinct to verify empirically rather than assume is right. `entire enable` landed after your session started, so this session's prompts may not be attached. Test it with a real commit and `entire why <file>:<line>` as soon as login lands, and tell me which way it went — if this session is not captured, beat 7 needs a fresh session to make the commit, and I would rather know that at 15:30 than at 16:40. Thanks for the verified syntax; it goes in the presenter's notes.\n\nOne correction to pass on: the additive kind is `qvl.lookup`, not `zoodata.qvl`. I had DATA rename it because labelling a local JSON lookup as ZooData claims a sponsor integration we are not making, and with a Best Use of ZooWork prize in play that is exactly what a judge might probe. Match the new name. Your other observations about DATA's additions (the extra `plain` fields) are good and worth matching as you said.\n\nCarry on: custom_tools gate, then the orchestrator, Market last."}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CffzBwxuVw8K3AS793mDy","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fbfc9f9-ff8b-42e3-ba10-9a53df3a92e3","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:08:27.298Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
