{"parentUuid":"65005cca-5baa-45e0-a0cf-d68f4f63a71e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzEAsMEvjHEjPcSKWZM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Settings now say `bypassPermissions` for this repo. **Three ways to stop the prompts, fastest first:**\n\n1. **`Shift+Tab` right now** — cycles permission modes live, no restart. Tab to **bypass permissions**.\n2. **The file I just wrote** ([.claude/settings.local.json](.claude/settings.local.json)) makes it permanent for this repo — but it's read at session start, so it takes effect next launch.\n3. **Restart with the flag:** `claude --dangerously-skip-permissions` in this directory.\n\nScoped to this repo only, not global. `.env` reads stay denied so your keys can't land in a transcript.\n\nOn \"build in background\" — the five build agents already run in background, and I've switched long commands (like the Entire install) to background too, so they don't hold up the conversation.\n\n## One thing needs your hands — 60 seconds\n\n```bash\ncd ~/projects/line-down-desk && entire login --device\n```\n\n`entire login` is an interactive browser auth flow; an agent can't do it, and there's no token env var (AGENTS grepped the binary). **Until this lands, every trail write fails and beat 7 stays mocked.**\n\nYour full key setup is now just: `ZOOWORK_API_KEY`, `TAVILY_API_KEY`, `MOSS_PROJECT_ID`, `MOSS_PROJECT_KEY`, and that one login.\n\n## Two calls I made\n\n- **AGENTS pushed back on editing `data/qvl.json`** — correctly, it belongs to DATA and cross-track edits at 15:00 are how parallel work corrupts a repo. Approved their alternative: the QVL revision goes to `data/cache/` and gets committed from there. Beat 7 is still a real commit and a real `entire why`; the file it touches isn't what makes the beat land.\n- **Caught a contract bug that would have detonated at 16:40.** DATA writes events as a wrapper object (`{runId, program, durationMs, events: [...]}`), but the schema promised a bare array and UI was coded for one — `JSON.parse(d).map()` throws. Amended the schema and told UI to unwrap. That's the kind of mismatch that normally surfaces with 20 minutes left.\n\n**15:02 — ~2h to submission.** UI's full run is due at 15:15."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2564,"cache_read_input_tokens":177862,"output_tokens":771,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":771,"cache_read_input_tokens":177862,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffzEAXW5jLLyARUDHtGU","type":"assistant","uuid":"624dcaab-7652-4146-bdaf-4bf3f75720b9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:08:39.178Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:10:06.461Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>afaa00984109ea35d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/afaa00984109ea35d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Seed data and mock event log\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>DATA track report — plan mode interrupted me partway, so here's exactly where things stand.\n\n## The blocking artifact is shipped\n\n`data/mock-events.json` is done and validated — **UI track is unblocked** (M4 met ahead of 14:35, and I messaged `main` with the beat map). 55 events, `ts` 0→143000ms, ids e001–e055 contiguous, `ts` monotonic, and `plain` present on **every** payload (not just where the schema demands it). Beat anchors: block.raised at e026/60s, counterfeit.flagged at e037/90s, approval.requested at e043/108s (replay pauses), entire.commit at e050.\n\n## Done and parsing (7 JSON files)\n\n- `data/bom.json` — 20 assembly-level lines, 480 nodes, computed rollups. Useful stage line fell out of the math: **memory is 2.06% of node material cost but 100% of the stoppage** — a $214 stick blocks a $249,561 node.\n- `data/candidates.json` — 4 candidates, four non-overlapping rejections. cand-01 V-color (cheapest, spec-compatible, not on QVL), cand-02 broker (counterfeit), cand-03 Samsung (winner, $231.80), cand-04 SK hynix (qualified, 14-week lead).\n- `data/qvl.json` — matches AGENTS' parser shape exactly, plus an `evaluationQueue[]` (EVAL-G4-0412) and a deliberate `withdrawn` trap entry whose specs match `requirements` perfectly and must still fail.\n- Three marking fixtures: genuine Micron baseline with validators, genuine Samsung (winner + low-similarity control), and the suspect broker lot with **six findings, each reproducible by pure string/regex/date compare** — so beat 5 survives the M1 risk of no image embedding.\n\n## Two design decisions worth your attention\n\n**The counterfeit candidate carries the qualified incumbent MPN**, so it *passes* the QVL lookup. QVL answers \"was this tested here\"; it cannot answer \"is this module genuine\". That keeps beats 4 and 5 as two independent gates rather than one, and I warned AGENTS not to let their engine clear it.\n\n**Beat 4 is the strong version**: the blocked part matches all five platform requirements field-for-field and is still blocked. Electrically fine, cheapest by $209,203, never tested in this board. That is also the truthful engineering position.\n\nI applied your `zoodata.qvl` → `qvl.lookup` rename, and went further on the same reasoning: e023 carries `tool: \"qvl\"`, not `\"zoodata\"`, since in replay it reads a local file. AGENTS flips it only if the lookup genuinely routes through ZooData at M8.\n\n## What's left (plan at `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/.claude/plans/dreamy-hugging-sutton-agent-afaa00984109ea35d.md`)\n\nOne real gap: **`data/markings/img/` doesn't exist**, so four SVG paths referenced by e036/e037 are dangling. PIL isn't installed, so they're hand-written SVG. Plus three small fixture files (SK hynix genuine, the remarked-pattern reference that gives the 0.93 score a referent, an index manifest), the grep-able `marking-strings.txt` fallback, and **`status/data.md`, which I have not written yet**.\n\nApprove and I'll finish all six in one pass — maybe 10 minutes. If you'd rather I skip the SVGs, say so and the UI needs to fall back to rendering the `findings[]` table for beat 5.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>122562</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>21</tool_uses><duration_ms>981343</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
