{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:10:34.793Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a9f9530c368f9676d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/a9f9530c368f9676d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"War room UI with replay engine\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I've stopped editing as instructed. Plan written to `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/.claude/plans/dreamy-hugging-sutton-agent-a9f9530c368f9676d.md`.\n\n## Status: UI track, ~70% to M5\n\n**On the coordinator's four asks — all already handled in code before the message arrived:**\n\n1. **Wrapper object** — `ui/lib/run.ts` has `normalizeRun()`: `Array.isArray(raw) ? [...raw] : raw.events`, ts-sorted, and it returns `runId` + `durationMs`. My status file said `Event[]`, but the loader I actually wrote tolerates both. Nothing throws.\n2. **`durationMs` / `program`** — both captured; `durationMs` is earmarked for the scrubber, `program` already renders in the alert panel.\n3. **`qvl.lookup`** — `ToolEvidence.tsx` case-falls `\"qvl.lookup\"` and `\"zoodata.qvl\"` into the same labelled evidence card (the file on disk still said `zoodata.qvl` when I first read it and `qvl.lookup` on the second read, so accepting both was necessary regardless).\n4. **`plain` everywhere** — plumbed through `types.ts`/`derive.ts` for `tool.call`, `tool.result`, `po.drafted`, `approval.requested` and `run.ended`, not just the schema-named events.\n\n**Also addressed from the earlier message:** counter primed from the 14:02 notice via `noticePrimeMs()` (parsed out of `runId`, clamped to 12h against a bad system clock, labelled \"exposure accrued since 14:02 allocation notice\"); Tavily results get a neutral source list plus an `illustrative · not retrieved` badge driven off `payload._illustrative`, with no fetch animation.\n\n**One thing I corrected in your data's favour:** the shipped `score: 0.93` is a match against the *known-remarked* cluster, so high means guilty — my gauge was inverted. The card now reads `remark-pattern match` / `confirmed remark` with the flag threshold at 85 exceeded, and flips its wording if a payload ever scores against the genuine reference instead.\n\n**Built:** scaffold + deps, design tokens, `useEventStream` (replay/live interchangeable, Space/R/→/Shift+→, → jumps between the 7 beats and cannot bypass the approval gate), `derive`, `AlertPanel`, `MoneyCounter`, `CounterfeitCard`, `BlockCard`, `ApprovalGate`, `ToolEvidence` (all 5 kinds + neutral fallback), `scripts/sync-data.mjs` (real log already synced to `public/events.json`).\n\n**Remaining:** 5 files — `MiscCards` (incl. the `$2,487,600` outcome hero), `RoomFeed`, `CaseFile`, `StageBar`, `app/page.tsx` — then typecheck, build, and screenshot the three money shots.\n\n⚠️ **Gap worth raising now:** `counterfeit.flagged.imageA/imageB` and all `moss.matches` thumbnails point at `data/markings/img/*.svg`, which **does not exist**. I generated placeholder marking SVGs and the card falls back to them on image error, so the hero shot composes — but those real assets are the single biggest remaining quality win on the X-Factor screenshot, and `sync-data.mjs` picks them up with zero code change.\n\nSay the word and I'll execute the plan.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>131211</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>59</tool_uses><duration_ms>994208</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:10:48.771Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a9dd0b82deda8a17d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01LQaoBYVovwKLbjkukYL6Ah</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/a9dd0b82deda8a17d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"ZooWork agents and BAND room\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Plan mode blocks further edits and neither `AskUserQuestion` nor `ExitPlanMode` is available to me, so here's the state and the plan. Plan file: `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/.claude/plans/dreamy-hugging-sutton-agent-a9dd0b82deda8a17d.md`\n\n## Done\n\n**Step 1 complete first, as instructed.** `npx skills add SerendipityOneInc/zoowork-sdk-skills` installed to `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/.agents/skills/zoowork-managed-agents` — it worked on Node v20.20.2 despite the 22.20+ note (the SDK itself only needs 20+). I read all 8 reference files and verified every signature against the installed `@zoowork-ai/sdk` 0.10.2 `dist/*.d.ts` rather than recalling them.\n\nFiles written:\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/agents/types.ts` — typed restatement of the frozen schema\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/agents/events.ts` — `EventLog` + pre-flight validator\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/agents/tools/qvl.ts` — the QVL engine\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/agents/tools/qvl.test.ts` — 7 test groups (written, not yet run)\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/agents/tools/tavily.ts` — cache-first search + `captureAll()`\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/status/agents.md`\n\nEntire CLI 0.11.3 installed, `entire enable` confirmed present, `entire why &lt;file&gt;:&lt;line&gt; --json` syntax verified from `entire agent-help`.\n\n## Three findings worth your attention\n\n**1. The ZooWork mechanism for beat 4 is better than a tool call — it's a real runtime pause.** `resource.custom_tools` are application-executed: the run emits `agent.custom_tool_use` and **halts inside the ZooWork runtime** until my process calls `resolveCustomToolCall`. RECON independently confirmed BAND has no gating primitive at all (zero hits for critic/veto/gate; its entire event vocabulary is five strings). So Engineering's veto is platform-enforced, not prompt convention — and that's the claim a judge can be invited to test.\n\n**2. I caught a contract divergence that would have surfaced at 16:40.** `data/mock-events.json` is a wrapper object (`{_comment, runId, program, durationMs, events}`), but the frozen schema said \"a run is `Event[]`\" and UI was coding against a bare array — `JSON.parse(file).map(...)` would have thrown. Coordinator has amended the schema and told UI to unwrap.\n\n**3. I declined to edit `data/qvl.json`** when instructed to, because it's DATA's file and outside my brief. Coordinator approved the alternative (write rev-E to `data/cache/`, commit that). Flagging because it was a deliberate refusal, not an oversight.\n\n## Blockers\n\n- **`entire login` is interactive** — browser or `--device` only; I grepped the binary and there is no token env var. Needs the user's hands; already escalated. Beat 7 degrades to a mocked hash without it.\n- **`entire enable` landed after my session started**, so this session's prompts may not be captured even once login lands. Needs empirical verification with a real commit — if it isn't captured, beat 7 needs a fresh session to make the commit.\n- **No sponsor keys present.** By design every adapter is cache/fixture-first, so a full valid run produces with zero keys. User needs exactly: `export ZOOWORK_API_KEY=...`, `export TAVILY_API_KEY=...`, plus `entire login --device`. Note `ZOOWORK_ORG_ID` and `ZOOWORK_AGENT_ID` do **not** exist — I grepped the shipped package; only `ZOOWORK_API_KEY`, `ZOOWORK_BASE_URL` and `ZOOWORK_WEBHOOK_SECRET` appear, and `BASE_URL` should stay unset.\n\n## Two open questions\n\n1. **`tool: \"zoodata\"` on the QVL `tool.call` has the same problem the renamed `kind` had.** The kind is now `qvl.lookup`, but the frozen enum for `tool.call.tool` is `\"tavily\" | \"moss\" | \"entire\" | \"zoodata\"` and DATA's `e023` sets `tool: \"zoodata\"` for this lookup — that field is what the UI renders as the tool badge, so it's the *more* visible claim. There's no `\"zoowork\"` in the enum. Extend it, or accept `zoodata` as a generic internal-lookup label?\n2. **Should the presenter attempt the vision OCR live?** It needs a vision-capable row to be `selectable` in `listModels()`, which I can't check without a key. Replay carries a known-good transcription either way, so the beat is safe — but it's a go/no-go someone should make before the 16:30 freeze.\n\n## Remaining (ordered, Market last per the cut ladder)\n\nRun the QVL test → fix `events.ts` (wrapper output, short `callId`s, `plain` fields) → `moss.ts` (wraps the MOSS Python spike, `--offline` fallback) → `entire.ts` → `zoowork.ts` (serial provisioning, model selection, custom-tool resolution loop) → 5 agent defs → `band.ts` orchestrator (typed turn-taking, structural two-gate veto) → `run.ts` CLI → Tavily capture → final status.\n\nI need plan mode lifted to continue — roughly 60% of the build remains and the orchestrator is the long pole.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>154804</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>54</tool_uses><duration_ms>992704</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
