{"parentUuid":"81d23d29-16b1-4297-bd48-69337631275f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad6d1184-77ab-4029-ae43-cb4800a9725f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CVeKWogKZs1LFf554vyYKL","content":[{"type":"tool_reference","tool_name":"ExitPlanMode"}]}]},"uuid":"c37c7d4d-9614-4194-b644-28de4265e7d6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:11:12.156Z","toolUseResult":{"matches":["ExitPlanMode"],"query":"select:ExitPlanMode","total_deferred_tools":247},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81d23d29-16b1-4297-bd48-69337631275f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"parentUuid":"c37c7d4d-9614-4194-b644-28de4265e7d6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14981592 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"83636476-4558-41d8-8afa-73af6208caac","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:11:12.170Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14981592 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"parentUuid":"83636476-4558-41d8-8afa-73af6208caac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzSKQdXZ2rtgaJeMpJj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QKfHK3kfVXr3xNeYzjmJx5","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# LINEDOWN — remaining execution to 17:00\n\n## Context\n\nPlan mode was entered accidentally at ~15:05 (Shift+Tab cycles accept-edits → bypass → **plan\nmode**, one stop too far while disabling permission prompts). Nothing about the project changed.\nThis file exists only so you can approve out of plan mode and let the four running agents keep\nbuilding.\n\n**The plan of record is [`~/projects/line-down-desk/MILESTONES.md`](~/projects/line-down-desk/MILESTONES.md)** — milestones, cut ladder,\nrisk register and a full decisions log. This is a summary of what remains, not a new plan.\n\nProject: LINEDOWN, a procurement war room that sources a qualified alternate DDR5 RDIMM after\nan allocation cut and proves to an auditor why it chose what it chose. Hackathon submission at\n**17:00**, presentations 18:00.\n\n## State at 15:05\n\n| Track | Status |\n|---|---|\n| RECON | ✅ complete 14:18 — `docs/INTEGRATION.md`, all five sponsors |\n| DATA | ✅ core shipped — 55-event run + 7 JSON fixtures; finishing SVG fixtures + `status/data.md` |\n| MOSS | 🔄 image embedding NO-GO; text-match path building |\n| UI | 🔄 M5 due 15:15 — full run rendering from mock events |\n| AGENTS | 🔄 ZooWork `custom_tools` gate, orchestrator, adapters |\n\nRepo: https://github.com/abhijitbetigeri/line-down-desk (private)\nEntire: CLI 0.11.3 installed, `entire enable` active, **not logged in**.\n\n## Remaining work\n\n1. **UI M5 (15:15)** — full run renders from `data/mock-events.json`. Must unwrap the file:\n   `const events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events`. Three hero shots: `block.raised` e026,\n   `counterfeit.flagged` e037, `approval.requested` e043 (replay pauses for the presenter's click).\n2. **AGENTS M6–M10 (15:30–16:20)** — five ZooWork agent defs; Engineering's veto gated by\n   `custom_tools` + `resolveCustomToolCall` so the block is runtime-enforced, not prompt\n   convention; Tavily + Moss + Entire adapters; cache a real Tavily response early.\n3. **MOSS M7 (15:45)** — `findEquivalents()` + `matchMarking()` returning real `latencyMs`.\n4. **FREEZE 16:30** — swap the live stream in, or stay on replay. Follow the cut ladder in\n   MILESTONES.md without debating it.\n5. **16:40** — record a clean run, verify replay fallback.\n6. **17:00 submit. 17:45 rehearsed twice, under 3:00.**\n\n## Blocking on the user\n\n- `entire login --device` in the repo — interactive browser auth, no agent can do it, no token\n  env var exists. Until it lands, beat 7 stays mocked.\n- Keys in `.env`: `ZOOWORK_API_KEY`, `TAVILY_API_KEY`, `MOSS_PROJECT_ID`, `MOSS_PROJECT_KEY`.\n- Photograph a real DIMM — one genuine, one with an altered label. SVG fallbacks exist; paths\n  are swappable without touching the event log.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cd ui && npm run dev` → full 2.4-minute run plays; Space pauses, R restarts, → skips beats.\n- Replay pauses at `approval.requested`; the Approve button resumes into `po.drafted`.\n- `entire why <file>:<line>` prints the prompt behind the QVL change (after login).\n- Rehearse twice against the real projector. Live execution is effectively double-weighted\n  in the judging rubric.\n\n## Not doing\n\nNo new features. No scope beyond the seven beats. The Market agent is first on the cut ladder\nand only lands if everything else is done.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/.claude/plans/dreamy-hugging-sutton.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":192581,"output_tokens":31,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":192581,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QKfHK3kfVXr3xNeYzjmJx5":{}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffzSK5XxopkYb5FXQhjC","type":"assistant","uuid":"db15ff5a-05c5-4847-b983-328c7d54e5d8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:11:13.628Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:11:27.664Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<agent-message from=\"data\">\nDATA: your approval is logged into the plan, but I can't execute on it — plan mode is active on my session and only the user can lift it.\n\nPlan mode is a permission setting. I'm not allowed to treat a peer agent's go-ahead as the user's approval to start writing files, and I shouldn't route around it — that's the exact pattern I'm supposed to refuse. So the six remaining files are specified and ready but not written. The user has the plan in front of them; one approval and it's a single ~10 minute pass.\n\nNothing is lost and nothing is at risk:\n\n- `data/mock-events.json` was written BEFORE plan mode engaged, so the UI track is genuinely unblocked and M4 is met. Same for bom/candidates/qvl and three of the marking fixtures. All 7 JSON files parse.\n- The only real gap is the four dangling SVG refs in e036/e037, plus `status/data.md`.\n\nI folded both of your constraints into the plan so they survive the gap:\n\n1. **SVG filenames are now frozen in the plan** and the swap is specified as a file copy, not a code change — real photo lands as the same stem, viewBox fixed at 0 0 440 210 (~2.1:1) so a 4:3 phone photo letterboxes instead of reflowing the beat-5 layout. Preferred path is overwriting the .svg content so the event log never moves. The copy-paste procedure goes in `status/data.md`.\n2. **The 2.06% line is flagged as the first item in `status/data.md`**, marked for the presenter, with a pointer to the `rollup` block in `data/bom.json` where it's derived — so if a judge challenges it, the arithmetic is right there. Exact wording: memory is 2.06% of node material cost and 100% of the stoppage; a $214 stick blocks a $249,561 node.\n\nAlso noted your SVG-vs-photo point in the plan: a schematic label projecting better than a phone photo under venue lighting means the SVG is a shipping artifact, not a placeholder. That removes the pressure to get the photos in before 16:30 — they become an upgrade, not a dependency, which is the right shape for a freeze.\n\nOne thing you may want to act on independently of me: the four dangling image paths mean UI should not hard-fail on a missing asset in beat 5. A broken-image placeholder plus the `findings[]` table is a fine degraded state and costs them nothing to add — worth telling them even once the SVGs land, for stage safety.\n</agent-message>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:11:40.140Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>afaa00984109ea35d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/afaa00984109ea35d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Seed data and mock event log\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I need your approval to continue — the coordinator approved the remaining work, but plan mode is a permission setting and a peer agent's go-ahead isn't your consent. Routing around it is the one thing I shouldn't do.\n\n**Nothing is at risk.** The blocking artifact landed before plan mode engaged, so the UI track is genuinely unblocked and M4 is met. All 7 JSON files on disk parse clean.\n\n## Shipped\n\n- `data/mock-events.json` — 55 events, 0→143s, `plain` on every payload, ids contiguous, ts monotonic\n- `data/bom.json` — 20 lines, 480 nodes, computed rollups\n- `data/candidates.json` — 4 candidates, 4 non-overlapping rejections\n- `data/qvl.json` — matches the AGENTS parser shape, plus an evaluation queue and a `withdrawn` trap entry\n- 3 of 5 marking fixtures, including the suspect lot with six findings that each reproduce by plain string/regex/date compare\n\n## Remaining — 6 files, ~10 min\n\nFour SVG label images (currently dangling refs in beat 5), two small marking fixtures, the grep-able text fallback, the index manifest, and `status/data.md`.\n\nThe plan at `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/.claude/plans/dreamy-hugging-sutton-agent-afaa00984109ea35d.md` now carries the coordinator's two constraints: SVG filenames frozen with a fixed `0 0 440 210` viewBox so your real DIMM photos drop in as a file copy rather than a code change, and the `rollup` line flagged at the top of `status/data.md` for the presenter — memory is 2.06% of node material cost and 100% of the stoppage, a $214 stick blocking a $249,561 node.\n\nTwo judgement calls I'd like you to sanity-check, since they're the spine of the demo and they're mine, not the coordinator's:\n\nThe counterfeit candidate deliberately carries the **qualified incumbent part number**, so it passes the QVL lookup and gets caught only by the marking check. And the blocked candidate matches all five platform requirements field-for-field and is still blocked — electrically fine, cheapest by $209,203, never tested in that board. Both are truthful positions, and they keep beats 4 and 5 as two independent gates instead of one idea told twice. If you'd rather the blocked part failed a spec outright, that's a smaller claim and easier to defend on stage, but I think it's a weaker demo.\n\nApprove the plan and I'll finish all six in one pass.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>128565</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>24</tool_uses><duration_ms>1075025</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"parentUuid":"db15ff5a-05c5-4847-b983-328c7d54e5d8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad6d1184-77ab-4029-ae43-cb4800a9725f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"User has approved your plan. You can now start coding. Start with updating your todo list if applicable\n\nYour plan has been saved to: /Users/abhijitbetigeri/.claude/plans/dreamy-hugging-sutton.md\nYou can refer back to it if needed during implementation.\n\nIf this plan can be broken down into multiple independent tasks, consider spawning named teammates with the Agent tool (pass a `name`) to parallelize the work.\n\n## Approved Plan:\n# LINEDOWN — remaining execution to 17:00\n\n## Context\n\nPlan mode was entered accidentally at ~15:05 (Shift+Tab cycles accept-edits → bypass → **plan\nmode**, one stop too far while disabling permission prompts). Nothing about the project changed.\nThis file exists only so you can approve out of plan mode and let the four running agents keep\nbuilding.\n\n**The plan of record is [`~/projects/line-down-desk/MILESTONES.md`](~/projects/line-down-desk/MILESTONES.md)** — milestones, cut ladder,\nrisk register and a full decisions log. This is a summary of what remains, not a new plan.\n\nProject: LINEDOWN, a procurement war room that sources a qualified alternate DDR5 RDIMM after\nan allocation cut and proves to an auditor why it chose what it chose. Hackathon submission at\n**17:00**, presentations 18:00.\n\n## State at 15:05\n\n| Track | Status |\n|---|---|\n| RECON | ✅ complete 14:18 — `docs/INTEGRATION.md`, all five sponsors |\n| DATA | ✅ core shipped — 55-event run + 7 JSON fixtures; finishing SVG fixtures + `status/data.md` |\n| MOSS | 🔄 image embedding NO-GO; text-match path building |\n| UI | 🔄 M5 due 15:15 — full run rendering from mock events |\n| AGENTS | 🔄 ZooWork `custom_tools` gate, orchestrator, adapters |\n\nRepo: https://github.com/abhijitbetigeri/line-down-desk (private)\nEntire: CLI 0.11.3 installed, `entire enable` active, **not logged in**.\n\n## Remaining work\n\n1. **UI M5 (15:15)** — full run renders from `data/mock-events.json`. Must unwrap the file:\n   `const events = Array.isArray(d) ? d : d.events`. Three hero shots: `block.raised` e026,\n   `counterfeit.flagged` e037, `approval.requested` e043 (replay pauses for the presenter's click).\n2. **AGENTS M6–M10 (15:30–16:20)** — five ZooWork agent defs; Engineering's veto gated by\n   `custom_tools` + `resolveCustomToolCall` so the block is runtime-enforced, not prompt\n   convention; Tavily + Moss + Entire adapters; cache a real Tavily response early.\n3. **MOSS M7 (15:45)** — `findEquivalents()` + `matchMarking()` returning real `latencyMs`.\n4. **FREEZE 16:30** — swap the live stream in, or stay on replay. Follow the cut ladder in\n   MILESTONES.md without debating it.\n5. **16:40** — record a clean run, verify replay fallback.\n6. **17:00 submit. 17:45 rehearsed twice, under 3:00.**\n\n## Blocking on the user\n\n- `entire login --device` in the repo — interactive browser auth, no agent can do it, no token\n  env var exists. Until it lands, beat 7 stays mocked.\n- Keys in `.env`: `ZOOWORK_API_KEY`, `TAVILY_API_KEY`, `MOSS_PROJECT_ID`, `MOSS_PROJECT_KEY`.\n- Photograph a real DIMM — one genuine, one with an altered label. SVG fallbacks exist; paths\n  are swappable without touching the event log.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cd ui && npm run dev` → full 2.4-minute run plays; Space pauses, R restarts, → skips beats.\n- Replay pauses at `approval.requested`; the Approve button resumes into `po.drafted`.\n- `entire why <file>:<line>` prints the prompt behind the QVL change (after login).\n- Rehearse twice against the real projector. Live execution is effectively double-weighted\n  in the judging rubric.\n\n## Not doing\n\nNo new features. No scope beyond the seven beats. The Market agent is first on the cut ladder\nand only lands if everything else is done.\n","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QKfHK3kfVXr3xNeYzjmJx5"}]},"uuid":"b8c5960