{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:12:34.518Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab2d6c1d0079879cb</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/ab2d6c1d0079879cb.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Moss multimodal go/no-go spike\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Plan mode is now active, so I'm stopping here — which is fine, because the task is complete and verified. No further changes are needed.\n\n## MOSS track — GO/NO-GO called (delivered inside the 25-minute window)\n\n**NO-GO on image embedding. GO on the text path — beat 5 works and is verified running.**\n\n### The answer to the critical question\n\nMoss is **text-only in practice**. I didn't rely on docs — I installed the SDK and introspected it:\n\n- `DocumentInfo` exposes exactly `(id, text, metadata, embedding, payload)`. Passing `image`, `image_path`, `image_bytes` or `audio` is **rejected**.\n- `client.query(name, query: str, options)` takes a **string**. No image overload.\n- Zero `image`/`clip`/`vision`/`multimodal` symbols anywhere in the shipped package.\n- Verified on **both** the stable `moss` 1.14.0 and the `inferedge-moss` 1.0.0b19 beta.\n- The clincher: Moss's own `usemoss/moss-image-search-demo` builds `DocumentInfo(id, text=&lt;COCO caption&gt;, metadata={url, image_id})`. It is text search with pictures attached — the pixels never reach Moss.\n\n### Gotchas that would each have cost someone 20+ minutes\n\n1. **Don't copy the install from Moss's own demos.** They pin `inferedge-moss` (a *beta*); the stable package is plain `moss` 1.14.0 with far more surface. Both install, which is the trap.\n2. **`QueryOptions` moved between packages** — in `moss_core` on the beta, top-level on stable. The spike tries stable then falls back.\n3. `@moss-dev/moss` (moss.dev homepage) is stale at 1.7.1; the README's `@moss-js/moss` is 1.15.0.\n4. `load_index()` is mandatory before `query()` — the #1 confusing failure.\n5. Errors are **bare `RuntimeError`**, including auth (HTTP 403). You can't catch auth separately from a missing index.\n\n### An unexpected find that may restore the photo on stage\n\n`moss&gt;=1.14` has a server-side parser with `ParseOptions(ocr_mode=\"full_ocr\")`. `ParseFileInput` accepts **only** PDF and DOCX — a JPEG is refused — but a JPEG *wrapped in a one-page PDF* is accepted, so Moss will OCR the photographed label itself. I implemented it in `spikes/moss/ocr_upgrade.py` with a dependency-free JPEG→PDF wrapper. **The PDF writer is verified** (macOS CoreGraphics parses the output at correct dimensions); the Moss OCR call is **unverified** without keys. It's opt-in and the default path doesn't depend on it. Caveat for the stage: parsing is a multi-second server round trip, so `parseMs` is returned separately from the query's `latencyMs` — don't add them or show parseMs as \"Moss latency\".\n\n### Verified working now, zero keys\n\n`python spikes/moss/demo.py --offline` passes, with schema conformance asserted against `docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md`:\n\n| Beat | Result | latencyMs |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3 `findEquivalents` | 4 true cross-vendor equivalents, near-misses filtered | 0.22 |\n| 5 `matchMarking` | **COUNTERFEIT** 0.875 vs genuine ref 0.807 | 0.20 |\n| control (genuine) | GENUINE 0.941 — no false positive | 0.17 |\n\nOne real retrieval finding worth keeping: the naive spec text mis-ranked — a Micron 5600-bin sibling beat the true Samsung equivalent. Fix was **delimiter-free compound spec tokens** (`CAP64GB SPD4800 FORMRDIMM`) plus dropping boilerplate, and `alpha=0.15` since a part number is a keyword problem, not a semantic one. Ranking is now monotonic, with the four genuine equivalents on top — which is what beats 4 and 5 need, since the cheapest options *are* real electrical equivalents and the block is about qualification, not specs.\n\n**Files written** (only within my lanes): `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/status/moss.md`, and `spikes/moss/{moss_partmatch.py,fixtures.py,demo.py,ocr_upgrade.py}`.\n\n**Two asks are logged in status/moss.md:** DATA should ship `data/markings/&lt;photo&gt;.jpg` + `&lt;photo&gt;.jpg.txt` pairs using my exact fixture paths (since `matchMarking` resolves a photo to text via sidecar and fails loudly rather than searching a filename); UI should treat an empty `equivalents` list as \"no equivalent found\", not an error.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>116752</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>47</tool_uses><duration_ms>1158203</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
