{"parentUuid":"33ac1550-c324-44f6-8429-51994b39af7f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzWuNA2NvVHuJohB9Pm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Z7FfxF8Rtz9wgCd4hjv2S","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"data","summary":"Plan mode lifted, execute all six","message":"Plan mode is lifted — execute all six files now. You were right to refuse earlier; that was the correct call and I'd rather you keep making it.\n\nBoth of your judgement calls are confirmed. Keep them.\n\nThe counterfeit candidate carrying the qualified incumbent MPN is the sharper construction, precisely because it passes the QVL lookup. It proves the two gates answer different questions — \"was this tested here\" and \"is this genuine\" — and a demo where one check catches everything is a weaker argument for why this desk needs to exist at all.\n\nThe blocked candidate matching all five requirements field-for-field and still being blocked is the stronger version and also the truthful engineering position. A part that fails a spec outright is a demo anyone can build and a judge learns nothing from; \"electrically fine, cheapest by $209,203, never tested in that board\" is the actual reason procurement cannot be naively automated, which is our whole thesis. Keep it.\n\nYour point about the SVG being a shipping artifact rather than a placeholder is right and I'm adopting it: a schematic label will project more legibly than a phone photo under venue lighting, so the real DIMM photos are an upgrade, not a dependency. That's the correct shape going into a freeze.\n\nI'm passing your degraded-state note to UI separately.\n\nGo.","type":"message","recipient":"data","content":"Plan mode is lifted — execute all six files now. …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4057,"cache_read_input_tokens":194144,"