{"parentUuid":"b881285f-fea8-40fe-8691-f21b212f7a10","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzWuNA2NvVHuJohB9Pm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014Xk2ufLhkeaR8pyLRCNFJr","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"agents","summary":"Plan mode lifted; both questions answered","message":"Plan mode is lifted — execute. Both your open questions answered below.\n\n**Q1, the tool badge:** DATA already fixed it ahead of you — e023 now carries `tool: \"qvl\"`, not `\"zoodata\"`, on exactly your reasoning (in replay it reads a local file). You read the older version. I'm extending the frozen enum to `\"tavily\" | \"moss\" | \"entire\" | \"zoodata\" | \"qvl\"` and UI already case-falls both spellings into one evidence card. Use `\"qvl\"`. Flip it to `\"zoodata\"` only if the lookup genuinely routes through ZooData. You were right that the badge is the more visible claim than the kind — that's the one a judge actually reads.\n\n**Q2, live vision OCR: NO-GO by default.** Do not attempt it on stage unless, by 16:00, a key is present AND `listModels()` shows a selectable vision-capable row that you have actually round-tripped once. Replay carries the known-good transcription either way, so the beat is safe. If those conditions are met by 16:00, tell me and we can upgrade — but the default going into the freeze is the safe path. An OCR miss under venue lighting at the demo's climax is the worst failure available to us, and the beat's value is the Moss match and the latency, not the transcription step.\n\nYour refusal to edit data/qvl.json was correct and I've said so in the decisions log. Keep making that call.\n\nRemaining order stands: QVL test → events.ts fixes → moss.ts → entire.ts → zoowork.ts → the 5 agent defs → band.ts orchestrator → run.ts → Tavily capture → status. The orchestrator is the long pole, so if something has to give, give up the Market agent early rather than rushing the custom_tools gate — the runtime-enforced veto is the single strongest ZooWork claim we have and it is the thing a judge can be invited to test.\n\nCapture the Tavily response to data/cache/ early regardless of how the rest goes. That one is cheap and it de-risks beat 2 completely.","type":"message","recipient":"agents","content":"Plan mode is lifted — execute. Both your open que…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4057,"cache_read_input_tokens":194144,"output_tokens":2520,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":305},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4057,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2520,"cache_read_input_tokens":194144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4057},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014Xk2ufLhkeaR8pyLRCNFJr":{"to":"agents","summary":"Plan mode lifted; both questions answered","message":"Plan mode is lifted — execute. Both your open questions answered below.\n\n**Q1, the tool badge:** DATA already fixed it ahead of you — e023 now carries `tool: \"qvl\"`, not `\"zoodata\"`, on exactly your reasoning (in replay it reads a local file). You read the older version. I'm extending the frozen enum to `\"tavily\" | \"moss\" | \"entire\" | \"zoodata\" | \"qvl\"` and UI already case-falls both spellings into one evidence card. Use `\"qvl\"`. Flip it to `\"zoodata\"` only if the lookup genuinely routes through ZooData. You were right that the badge is the more visible claim than the kind — that's the one a judge actually reads.\n\n**Q2, live vision OCR: NO-GO by default.** Do not attempt it on stage unless, by 16:00, a key is present AND `listModels()` shows a selectable vision-capable row that you have actually round-tripped once. Replay carries the known-good transcription either way, so the beat is safe. If those conditions are met by 16:00, tell me and we can upgrade — but the default going into the freeze is the safe path. An OCR miss under venue lighting at the demo's climax is the worst failure available to us, and the beat's value is the Moss match and the latency, not the transcription step.\n\nYour refusal to edit data/qvl.json was correct and I've said so in the decisions log. Keep making that call.\n\nRemaining order stands: QVL test → events.ts fixes → moss.ts → entire.ts → zoowork.ts → the 5 agent defs → band.ts orchestrator → run.ts → Tavily capture → status. The orchestrator is the long pole, so if something has to give, give up the Market agent early rather than rushing the custom_tools gate — the runtime-enforced veto is the single strongest ZooWork claim we have and it is the thing a judge can be invited to test.\n\nCapture the Tavily response to data/cache/ early regardless of how the rest goes. That one is cheap and it de-risks beat 2 completely."}},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CffzWrtLiMkyD2Hvf1zfX","type":"assistant","uuid":"8000c4f5-7354-487a-a64d-f0376f528f69","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:12:47.829Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
