{"parentUuid":"9aee7b98-bc71-414d-92e3-496b27919323","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzZaatjVRhecSQEMBoU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D8SiGyQJjnzNxUSjwZwQq9","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ui","summary":"Empty equivalents is a state, not an error","message":"One small ask from the MOSS track: treat an empty `equivalents` array in `moss.partmatch` as a legitimate \"no equivalent found\" state, not an error or an empty crash.\n\nIt's a real outcome in sourcing — sometimes nothing qualifies — and rendering it as a clean \"no cross-vendor equivalent found\" card costs you five minutes and removes a failure mode on stage.\n\nFor context, MOSS is done and verified offline with zero keys: beat 3 returns 4 true cross-vendor equivalents at 0.22ms, beat 5 scores the counterfeit at 0.875 against the remarked cluster with a genuine control at 0.941 and no false positive. So the latency numbers you render are real measurements, not decoration — worth showing with confidence.\n\nOne caveat if an OCR upgrade path ever lands: `parseMs` is a separate multi-second server round trip and must never be added to `latencyMs` or labelled \"Moss latency\". Keep those two numbers distinct if you ever see both.\n\nOtherwise unchanged — finish the five files.","type":"message","recipient":"ui","content":"One small ask from the MOSS track: treat an empty…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5213,"cache_read_input_tokens":198201,"output_tokens":3183,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":727},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5213,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3183,"cache_read_input_tokens":198201,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5213},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01D8SiGyQJjnzNxUSjwZwQq9":{"to":"ui","summary":"Empty equivalents is a state, not an error","message":"One small ask from the MOSS track: treat an empty `equivalents` array in `moss.partmatch` as a legitimate \"no equivalent found\" state, not an error or an empty crash.\n\nIt's a real outcome in sourcing — sometimes nothing qualifies — and rendering it as a clean \"no cross-vendor equivalent found\" card costs you five minutes and removes a failure mode on stage.\n\nFor context, MOSS is done and verified offline with zero keys: beat 3 returns 4 true cross-vendor equivalents at 0.22ms, beat 5 scores the counterfeit at 0.875 against the remarked cluster with a genuine control at 0.941 and no false positive. So the latency numbers you render are real measurements, not decoration — worth showing with confidence.\n\nOne caveat if an OCR upgrade path ever lands: `parseMs` is a separate multi-second server round trip and must never be added to `latencyMs` or labelled \"Moss latency\". Keep those two numbers distinct if you ever see both.\n\nOtherwise unchanged — finish the five files."}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CffzZaCpgMuGNF8XCWDa2","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f9f7421-8667-4364-ae26-a41c720d318b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:13:14.253Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"parentUuid":"5f9f7421-8667-4364-ae26-a41c720d318b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad6d1184-77ab-4029-ae43-cb4800a9725f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D8SiGyQJjnzNxUSjwZwQq9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Message queued for delivery to ui at its next tool round.\",\"pin\":{\"id\":\"a9f9530c368f9676d\",\"name\":\"ui\",\"ref\":\"10b87f\"}}"}]}]},"uuid":"94b8a31c-c9ed-4179-a2b3-0e76f10ffca7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:13:14.345Z","toolUseResult":{"success":true,"message":"Message queued for delivery to ui at its next tool round.","pin":{"id":"a9f9530c368f9676d","name":"ui","ref":"10b87f"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5f9f7421-8667-4364-ae26-a41c720d318b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"parentUuid":"94b8a31c-c9ed-4179-a2b3-0e76f10ffca7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffzZaatjVRhecSQEMBoU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ALA4MEtYToizmLnErsEaMz","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Presentation script and stage notes","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"pitch","prompt":"You are the PITCH track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Submission 17:00, presentations 18:00, 3 minutes on stage. Write the presentation script and stage notes. Deliver by 16:15.\n\nRead these first: MILESTONES.md (the 7-beat demo spine, decisions log, cut ladder), docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md, data/bom.json, data/candidates.json, status/data.md and status/moss.md. The event log data/mock-events.json has exact ts timings for every beat — your narration must fit them.\n\nJudging criteria, weighted as written: Approach & Idea (viable, creative, real-world/business viable), Technical Execution (robust, functional, sophisticated — AND \"able to execute primary features live\", which is asked TWICE so treat live execution as double-weighted), Presentation, Design (user-friendly, thoughtfully designed), X-Factor (surprise, delight, stand out). Two prizes: Best Use of ZooWork, and People's Choice.\n\nDeliver docs/PITCH.md containing:\n\n1. **The 3-minute script**, timed against real event timings, with stage directions. Beats: alert + money counter (ts 0) → Tavily pricing (12s) → Moss part matching at 0.22ms (29s) → ENGINEERING BLOCKS (60s) → COUNTERFEIT CAUGHT (90s) → presenter clicks Approve (108s) → Entire commit (125s) → close (143s). Mark exactly where the presenter clicks, pauses, and shuts up to let the screen work.\n2. **The opening line and the closing line, written to be memorised.** The close must land $2,487,600 saved.\n3. **A one-paragraph \"what is this\" for judges who arrive mid-demo.**\n4. **The Q&A sheet** — anticipate hard questions and give honest answers. Must cover: why a manufacturer at a commerce hackathon (answer: this is the buy side of B2B commerce, $2M of POs decided by agents); is the Engineering block real (yes, ZooWork custom_tools halts the run inside the runtime until our backend calls resolveCustomToolCall — it is platform-enforced, not prompt convention, and a judge can be invited to test it); is this replay or live (answer honestly — audit replay of a sourcing decision is exactly what IATF 16949 traceability requires, so it is a real feature, not a cop-out); module-level vs die-level substitution (we source an alternate MODULE, never substitute DRAM die); where the numbers come from.\n5. **Sponsor attribution lines** — one sentence each for ZooWork, Moss, Tavily, BAND, Entire, stating what each genuinely does in the system. Be precise: Moss has no image embedding so beat 5 is text matching over markings; BAND has no native veto so the gate is ZooWork's. Do not overclaim any sponsor — an overclaim that collapses under a question costs more than the claim is worth.\n\nCRITICAL constraints:\n- The best line available is in status/data.md: memory is 2.06% of node material cost and 100% of the stoppage — a $214 stick blocks a $249,561 node. Build the opening around it.\n- The pitch must be legible to a judge who does not know what a QVL is. Every piece of jargon gets a plain-language gloss the first time it is said.\n- Keep the buyer a manufacturer with a BOM and a ship date. Never let it read as commodity trading.\n- Never instruct the presenter to claim something we have not verified. If a capability is uncertain, write the honest version.\n\nAlso write a one-page docs/DEMO-RUNBOOK.md: exact commands to start the demo, keyboard controls (Space pause, R restart, right-arrow skip beats), what to do if a beat fails mid-demo, and the degraded-path fallbacks from the cut ladder.\n\nThe user is offline for about an hour, so make your own calls and note any assumption in the doc rather than waiting. Write only to docs/PITCH.md, docs/DEMO-RUNBOOK.md and status/pitch.md."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5213,"cache_read_input_tokens":198201,"output_tokens":3183,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":727},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5213,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3183,"cache_read_input_tokens":198201,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5213},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ALA4MEtYToizmLnErsEaMz":{"description":"Presentation script and stage notes","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"pitch","prompt":"You are the PITCH track for a hackathon project at /Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk. Submission 17:00, presentations 18:00, 3 minutes on stage. Write the presentation script and stage notes. Deliver by 16:15.\n\nRead these first: MILESTONES.md (the 7-beat demo spine, decisions log, cut ladder), docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md, data/bom.json, data/candidates.json, status/data.md and status/moss.md. The event log data/mock-events.json has exact ts timings for every beat — your narration must fit them.\n\nJudging criteria, weighted as written: Approach & Idea (viable, creative, real-world/business viable), Technical Execution (robust, functional, sophisticated — AND \"able to execute primary features live\", which is asked TWICE so treat live execution as double-weighted), Presentation, Design (user-friendly, thoughtfully designed), X-Factor (surprise, delight, stand out). Two prizes: Best Use of ZooWork, and People's Choice.\n\nDeliver docs/PITCH.md containing:\n\n1. **The 3-minute script**, timed against real event timings, with stage directions. Beats: alert + money counter (ts 0) → Tavily pricing (12s) → Moss part matching at 0.22ms (29s) → ENGINEERING BLOCKS (60s) → COUNTERFEIT CAUGHT (90s) → presenter clicks Approve (108s) → Entire commit (125s) → close (143s). Mark exactly where the presenter clicks, pauses, and shuts up to let the screen work.\n2. **The opening line and the closing line, written to be memorised.** The close must land $2,487,600 saved.\n3. **A one-paragraph \"what is this\" for judges who arrive mid-demo.**\n4. **The Q&A sheet** — anticipate hard questions and give honest answers. Must cover: why a manufacturer at a commerce hackathon (answer: this is the buy side of B2B commerce, $2M of POs decided by agents); is the Engineering block real (yes, ZooWork custom_tools halts the run inside the runtime until our backend calls resolveCustomToolCall — it is platform-enforced, not prompt convention, and a judge can be invited to test it); is this replay or live (answer honestly — audit replay of a sourcing decision is exactly what IATF 16949 traceability requires, so it is a real feature, not a cop-out); module-level vs die-level substitution (we source an alternate MODULE, never substitute DRAM die); where the numbers come from.\n5. **Sponsor attribution lines** — one sentence each for ZooWork, Moss, Tavily, BAND, Entire, stating what each genuinely does in the system. Be precise: Moss has no image embedding so beat 5 is text matching over markings; BAND has no native veto so the gate is ZooWork's. Do not overclaim any sponsor — an overclaim that collapses under a question costs more than the claim is worth.\n\nCRITICAL constraints:\n- The best line available is in status/data.md: memory is 2.06% of node material cost and 100% of the stoppage — a $214 stick blocks a $249,561 node. Build the opening around it.\n- The pitch must be legible to a judge who does not know what a QVL is. Every piece of jargon gets a plain-language gloss the first time it is said.\n- Keep the buyer a manufacturer with a BOM and a ship date. Never let it read as commodity trading.\n- Never instruct the presenter to claim something we have not verified. If a capability is uncertain, write the honest version.\n\nAlso write a one-page docs/DEMO-RUNBOOK.md: exact commands to start the demo, keyboard controls (Space pause, R restart, right-arrow skip beats), what to do if a beat fails mid-demo, and the degraded-path fallbacks from the cut ladder.\n\nThe user is offline for about an hour, so make your own calls and note any assumption in the doc rather than waiting. Write only to docs/PITCH.md, docs/DEMO-RUNBOOK.md and status/pitch.md."}},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CffzZaCpgMuGNF8XCWDa2","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5ecd498-404b-4e53-89d1-2b9631525bce","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:13:35.501Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
