ting what each genuinely does in the system. Be precise: Moss has no image embedding so beat 5 is text matching over markings; BAND has no native veto so the gate is ZooWork's. Do not overclaim any sponsor — an overclaim that collapses under a question costs more than the claim is worth.\n\nCRITICAL constraints:\n- The best line available is in status/data.md: memory is 2.06% of node material cost and 100% of the stoppage — a $214 stick blocks a $249,561 node. Build the opening around it.\n- The pitch must be legible to a judge who does not know what a QVL is. Every piece of jargon gets a plain-language gloss the first time it is said.\n- Keep the buyer a manufacturer with a BOM and a ship date. Never let it read as commodity trading.\n- Never instruct the presenter to claim something we have not verified. If a capability is uncertain, write the honest version.\n\nAlso write a one-page docs/DEMO-RUNBOOK.md: exact commands to start the demo, keyboard controls (Space pause, R restart, right-arrow skip beats), what to do if a beat fails mid-demo, and the degraded-path fallbacks from the cut ladder.\n\nThe user is offline for about an hour, so make your own calls and note any assumption in the doc rather than waiting. Write only to docs/PITCH.md, docs/DEMO-RUNBOOK.md and status/pitch.md.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/a0e386646fb2e3e81.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c5ecd498-404b-4e53-89d1-2b9631525bce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
