{"parentUuid":"26a62ee5-fb77-456b-aa72-06cc64139a3d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg3xANqtHwMxY8E3vKKD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**15:40 status** — written into [MILESTONES.md](projects/line-down-desk/MILESTONES.md) so you can orient in 30 seconds when you're back.\n\n**What happened while you were away:** all four agents hit a simultaneous infrastructure stall at ~15:30 — a watchdog timeout, not a work failure. Resumed at 15:35 with tightened scope.\n\n**Done:** RECON (all five sponsor APIs, source-verified), MOSS (verified offline, zero keys — counterfeit scores 0.875 vs genuine control 0.941, no false positive, ~0.2ms), DATA's seven JSON fixtures, and most UI components.\n\n**The one gap that matters:** `ui/app/page.tsx` doesn't exist, so nothing mounts yet. UI is writing it first. If it stalls again I'll write it by hand — every component it needs is already on disk.\n\n**Scope cuts I made without you**, given you're offline and no keys are coming:\n- AGENTS now optimises for a complete valid run **produced offline** rather than a half-finished live path we can't test. A second independently-produced run is worth more than untestable integration code.\n- Market agent dropped entirely. `entire.ts` stubbed — it needs your login.\n- Started a **pitch agent**: 3-minute script timed to the real event timings, plus a demo runbook and a Q&A sheet. That's the best use of an hour where no one can type keys.\n\n**Waiting on you when you're back (~5 min of work, all upgrades not dependencies):**\n1. `entire login --device` — unblocks beat 7's real trail\n2. Four keys in [.env](.env)\n3. DIMM photos — though DATA made a good call here: a schematic SVG label likely projects *better* than a phone photo under venue lighting, so these are now optional polish\n\nYou'll land right at the 16:30 freeze. I'll have the full picture ready."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":215218,"output_tokens":632,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1147,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":215218,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1147},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfg3xA411eKVPfLhBQT3P","type":"assistant","uuid":"344318e2-d549-4d8e-af23-3cc3275d211c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:57:28.159Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:03:22.467Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0e386646fb2e3e81</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01QQt9TNmBrf5Nd3urDfuPHv</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/a0e386646fb2e3e81.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Presentation script and stage notes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Delivered at 16:05, ahead of the 16:15 gate.\n\n## Written\n\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/docs/PITCH.md`\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/docs/DEMO-RUNBOOK.md`\n- `/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/status/pitch.md`\n\nNothing else touched.\n\n## The script fits 3:00 with 3 seconds of margin\n\n0:00–0:12 opening line on a static board → press Space → run plays `ts 0 → 143000` (2:35) + ~4s approval pause → close at 2:39–2:57. Every beat the brief named maps to a real `ts` in `data/mock-events.json`. One correction: the brief said Entire commits at 125s; the actual `tool.call` is 123s, hash 128s, `policy.committed` 130.5s. Script is written to the real numbers. Narration is paced to word counts at 150 wpm, and the three never-cut beats get written-in silences — 4 seconds on the block, 5 on the counterfeit, and a single 9-word line before the Approve click.\n\n## The arithmetic checks out\n\n`status/data.md` doesn't exist, so I re-derived the opening from `bom.json`'s `rollup` rather than trusting the quote: $2,465,280 ÷ $119,789,472 = 2.058% → 2.06%; $119,789,472 ÷ 480 = $249,561.40; `BOM-0020.unitCostUsd` = $214.00. Also verified $2,487,600 = $1,785,600 (1,240/min × 1,440) + $702,000, plus the $209,203 block cost and the $1,068,134.40 PO. The open and close are the same sentence twice — deliberate, for People's Choice recall.\n\n## One real conflict, handled honestly\n\nThe brief asked the presenter to say \"0.22 ms\" at beat 3. The event log carries `latencyMs: 6` and `8`, and its `plain` strings say so out loud; 0.22 ms is `status/moss.md`'s measured local figure. I would not write a number the audience can't read off the screen, so the script says \"single-digit milliseconds\" and instructs the presenter to speak what the UI renders. I messaged the DATA track to reconcile it before the 16:30 freeze and said I'll re-cut beat 3 if they move the log to 0.22.\n\n## Other calls made while you were offline\n\n- **Live vs replay branches only in Q&amp;A** (Q3/Q10) — narration is word-identical either way, so the M11 freeze doesn't touch the script.\n- **BAND gets a drop rule, not a soft claim.** §5 states plainly that BAND has no veto and the gate is ZooWork's. If M8 misses the freeze, the sentence comes out entirely — four precise attributions beat five with one aspirational, especially with ZooWork being the named prize. Note: `README.md`'s \"a Critic that can block\" contradicts RECON's SDK read and should be fixed by whoever owns that file; I flagged it rather than editing cross-track.\n- **Illustrative pricing is disclosed proactively** in Q5, not defended when caught — the data files' own comments say so.\n- **Beat 7 is terminal-only**, pre-opened; the runbook forbids clicking the blame URL.\n\nQ&amp;A covers 13 questions including all five you specified, plus the module-vs-die answer (and the HBM-is-the-cause-not-the-part follow-up, which is where the one industry expert in the room will probe). Jargon glosses are inline on first use — QVL gets \"the list of parts actually tested in this exact server, not parts that fit on paper,\" and IATF 16949 is held back for Q&amp;A where there's time to explain it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>103743</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>21</tool_uses><duration_ms>403019</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
