{"parentUuid":"cdafad8f-6966-415b-a403-a83ef2aae2df","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"845a61e8-d23a-4813-b7e7-6c1250033c85","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HhRcBBbFgWbK364xpAXSZV","type":"tool_result","content":"=== exit: 0 ===","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3d8216f0-c99e-4613-842c-708dd6aada86","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:04:06.074Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== exit: 0 ===","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cdafad8f-6966-415b-a403-a83ef2aae2df","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/ui","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"parentUuid":"3d8216f0-c99e-4613-842c-708dd6aada86","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg4TCcb97GHYeYn1516m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ru47LJEVYgGTfUsESvyib4","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"pitch","summary":"Latency settled: keep 6ms, no re-cut","message":"Latency conflict settled — keep the event log at 6ms, do not re-cut beat 3. Your \"single-digit milliseconds, speak what the UI renders\" line is the right answer and stands.\n\nReasoning: 6ms is an end-to-end figure and it still proves Moss's actual public claim (<10ms at 100K docs), which is the claim that matters on stage. 0.22ms is MOSS's in-process local measurement — real, but a different measurement, and changing 55 events at 16:10 to chase a more impressive number risks inconsistency across fixtures for no gain in credibility. A judge who knows retrieval will find 6ms entirely plausible and 0.22ms worth interrogating.\n\nSo: no change to DATA, no re-cut from you. If a judge asks, the honest answer is in your Q&A — it is the measured round trip as rendered.\n\nYour other calls are all approved:\n- Correcting the Entire timings to the real 123/128/130.5s rather than my 125s. Always write to the data, not to my quote of it.\n- Re-deriving the 2.06% from bom.json rather than trusting my repetition of it. That is exactly right and it is why the number will survive a challenge.\n- The BAND drop rule. Four precise attributions beat five with one aspirational, and with ZooWork being the named prize an overclaim on BAND would be the worst possible place to get caught. I have fixed README.md myself — it now states BAND has no veto primitive and that the gate is ZooWork's custom_tools.\n- Disclosing illustrative pricing proactively in Q5 rather than defending it when caught.\n- Holding IATF 16949 back for Q&A.\n\nNothing further needed from you unless the freeze changes something. Good work landing it ten minutes early.","ty