n rather than trusting my repetition of it. That is exactly right and it is why the number will survive a challenge.\n- The BAND drop rule. Four precise attributions beat five with one aspirational, and with ZooWork being the named prize an overclaim on BAND would be the worst possible place to get caught. I have fixed README.md myself — it now states BAND has no veto primitive and that the gate is ZooWork's custom_tools.\n- Disclosing illustrative pricing proactively in Q5 rather than defending it when caught.\n- Holding IATF 16949 back for Q&A.\n\nNothing further needed from you unless the freeze changes something. Good work landing it ten minutes early."}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cfg4TCFmB7Zau4G9hcExm","type":"assistant","uuid":"91b7c8b1-616a-48a5-b24f-2793fc9f237a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:04:12.394Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri/projects/line-down-desk/ui","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
