{"parentUuid":"b560d819-524d-4569-b7c8-4fa636b3823b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg54TFtDAzLu56d8QrQo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pek57PkFtCb4Xp5h46mEyF","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ui","summary":"Verify in browser, screenshot three shots","message":"Two things, both urgent — it is 16:15 and freeze is 16:30.\n\n**1. PORT CONFLICT — this is a stage risk.** Ports 3000 and 3001 are both occupied on this machine by other apps (3000 is something called \"Mise OS\"). Our dev server came up on **3002**. I nearly reported a false positive because I curled 3000 and got someone else's app. Make sure nothing in our code, README or scripts hardcodes 3000, and if you can, pin our dev script to a port we control so the presenter is never guessing on stage. Whatever you decide, state the real URL in status/ui.md.\n\n**2. Verify it actually plays, in a real browser.** Typecheck passes clean and the server returns HTTP 200 with the right title, but the body is ~6KB of shell — all the content is client-rendered, so nothing I can do from the shell proves the replay works. You own this and you have the context.\n\nConfirm specifically:\n- the run auto-plays (or that the presenter's first keystroke starts it) and reaches run.ended\n- Space pauses, R restarts, → skips beats\n- the approval gate at e043 genuinely halts the run and the Approve button is **clickable with a mouse** — the presenter may not have a keyboard hand free on stage\n- the three money shots compose: block e026, counterfeit e037 with both SVG labels side by side (data/markings/img/ now exists, four files), and the $2,487,600 outcome hero\n- no console errors that would show up on a projector\n\nThen screenshot those three. The screenshots are the submission artifact if the live run has any trouble at 18:00, so they are not optional polish.\n\nIf anything is broken, fix the smallest thing that makes the beat compose and tell me — do not start a refactor at 16:15.","type":"message","recipient":"ui","content":"Two things, both urgent — it is 16:15 and freeze …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":674,"cache_read_input_tokens":224381,"output_tokens":1758,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":551},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":674,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1758,"cache_read_input_tokens":224381,"cache_creation_input_tokens":674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":674},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Pek57PkFtCb4Xp5h46mEyF":{"to":"ui","summary":"Verify in browser, screenshot three shots","message":"Two things, both urgent — it is 16:15 and freeze is 16:30.\n\n**1. PORT CONFLICT — this is a stage risk.** Ports 3000 and 3001 are both occupied on this machine by other apps (3000 is something called \"Mise OS\"). Our dev server came up on **3002**. I nearly reported a false positive because I curled 3000 and got someone else's app. Make sure nothing in our code, README or scripts hardcodes 3000, and if you can, pin our dev script to a port we control so the presenter is never guessing on stage. Whatever you decide, state the real URL in status/ui.md.\n\n**2. Verify it actually plays, in a real browser.** Typecheck passes clean and the server returns HTTP 200 with the right title, but the body is ~6KB of shell — all the content is client-rendered, so nothing I can do from the shell proves the replay works. You own this and you have the context.\n\nConfirm specifically:\n- the run auto-plays (or that the presenter's first keystroke starts it) and reaches run.ended\n- Space pauses, R restarts, → skips beats\n- the approval gate at e043 genuinely halts the run and the Approve button is **clickable with a mouse** — the presenter may not have a keyboard hand free on stage\n- the three money shots compose: block e026, counterfeit e037 with both SVG labels side by side (data/markings/img/ now exists, four files), and the $2,487,600 outcome hero\n- no console errors that would show up on a projector\n\nThen screenshot those three. The screenshots are the submission artifact if the live run has any trouble at 18:00, so they are not optional polish.\n\nIf anything is broken, fix the smallest thing that makes the beat compose and tell me — do not start a refactor at 16:15."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfg54SvnWTXc9pj2vE6Zo","type":"assistant","uuid":"cabe549b-8bb4-4ef2-8dc7-b0115b1ca413","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:12:10.512Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
