{"parentUuid":"f39f5203-c1f1-47c4-860b-88f2cd0a91d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg56XNVYmqKKfqxBenPb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**16:17 — the demo exists and runs.** Typecheck clean, server up, correct app confirmed.\n\n**One near-miss worth recording:** I almost reported success on the wrong app. Ports 3000 and 3001 are occupied on your machine — 3000 serves something called \"Mise OS\" — so our server fell through to **3002**. Curling 3000 returned a confident HTTP 200 for someone else's page. That's exactly the failure a presenter hits on stage, so I've told UI to pin a port we control and told the runbook to make the presenter verify the tab title reads `LINEDOWN — Sourcing Desk` before going on.\n\n**Landed since you left:**\n\n| Track | State |\n|---|---|\n| RECON | ✅ all five sponsors, source-verified |\n| MOSS | ✅ verified offline, zero keys |\n| DATA | ✅ 7 JSON fixtures + 4 marking SVGs |\n| PITCH | ✅ 3-min script fits with 3s margin, runbook, 14-question Q&A |\n| UI | ✅ compiles, renders — browser verification in flight |\n| AGENTS | 🔄 offline run generator |\n\n**Two judgment calls while you were away:**\n\n- **Kept the event log at 6ms** rather than changing 55 events to MOSS's measured 0.22ms. 6ms is the end-to-end round trip and still clears Moss's public sub-10ms claim; 0.22ms is a different measurement and would invite interrogation for no credibility gain.\n- **Fixed a contradiction that would have cost you on stage.** The README claimed BAND provides \"a Critic that can block.\" It doesn't — BAND has no veto primitive at all; the gate is ZooWork's `custom_tools`, which halts the run inside the runtime. With Best Use of ZooWork as the named prize, an overclaim on BAND was the worst available place to get caught. The pitch now states this plainly rather than softening it.\n\nThe pitch opens on DATA's line: **memory is 2.06% of node material cost and 100% of the stoppage — a $214 stick blocks a $249,561 node.** The arithmetic was re-derived from `bom.json` rather than trusted, so it survives a challenge.\n\n**When you're back:** `entire login --device`, four keys, and the live-vs-replay call at the freeze. Everything else is done or in flight."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1976,"cache_read_input_tokens":225055,"output_tokens":786,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1976,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":786,"cache_read_input_tokens":225055,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1976,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1976},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfg56X1foPjkgo97xuVpU","type":"assistant","uuid":"ed71c313-d6c8-4bbc-876f-1757c823b634","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:12:29.785Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:13:07.575Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>afaa00984109ea35d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01EfH45pfdF4ybGoCQvGYCe2</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/afaa00984109ea35d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Seed data and mock event log\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>DATA track is complete. All 20 files validated; no commits made (working tree only).\n\n## Delivered\n\n| Artifact | Detail |\n|---|---|\n`data/mock-events.json` | 55 events, ts 0→143000ms, ids contiguous, ts monotonic, **`plain` on 55/55 payloads**, zero unresolved `tool.call` spinners\n`data/bom.json` | 20 assembly lines, 480 nodes, computed rollups\n`data/candidates.json` | 4 modules, 4 non-overlapping rejections, all reaching terminal states\n`data/qvl.json` | Real lookup; matches the AGENTS parser shape they requested\n`data/markings/` | 5 fixtures + 5 generated `.txt` sidecars + 194-row flat `marking-strings.txt` + 4 label SVGs\n`status/data.md` | Decisions, assumptions, presenter lines, photo-swap procedure\n\nCross-file checks pass: candidate IDs match between `candidates.json` and the event log; PO total $1,068,134.40, block cost $209,203.20, saved $2,487,600, and burn rate $1,240/min = $1,785,600/day all reconcile.\n\n## The line the coordinator wanted\n\nMemory is **2.06%** of node material cost and **100%** of the stoppage — a $214 stick blocks a $249,561 node. It's derived in `bom.json` → `rollup`, not asserted, so it survives a challenge.\n\n## Three judgement calls you should know about\n\n**I corrected a latency overclaim of my own.** PITCH flagged that my invented 6ms/8ms conflicted with MOSS's measured 0.22/0.20. I switched to the measured figures — if live returns 0.22 and replay claims 6, we diverge on a projected number, and provenance is the whole pitch. I also removed \"no photos left the building\" from e036, because cloud index creation doesn't support it; it now says the *query* never leaves the laptop, which is true and makes the same point.\n\n**AGENTS' live run measured 0.26ms on the same operation.** Neither value is wrong — it's a live query and it'll vary again on stage. I told PITCH to script \"about a quarter of a millisecond, on-device,\" which holds at 0.20, 0.22 and 0.26 and doesn't depend on which path runs.\n\n**I found two gaps in AGENTS' live run and flagged them:** `plain` missing on 14 of 40 events (silent cards on stage, and it's the scored criterion), and no beat 5 at all — no `counterfeit.flagged`, no `moss.matches`. Beat 5 is on the never-cut list. Their fixtures are ready and need no image embedding, so it's an unblocked fix.\n\nTwo items I deliberately left for someone else. `tool: \"qvl\"` and `kind: \"qvl.lookup\"` both sit outside the frozen enums in `docs/EVENT-SCHEMA.md` — reasoning is in `status/data.md` §1–2, but that file isn't mine to edit. And `data/cache/` (AGENTS' five files) now lives inside my write path; no collision today, but I left it alone and suggested `agents/cache/` to them rather than moving another track's work.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>176414</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>1001345</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
