{"parentUuid":"0fbf4d9a-a2b5-44f5-ba15-823013b72c0f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14940712 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5ad14782-3bca-4849-b895-7feeb71cf451","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:14:07.260Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14940712 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"parentUuid":"5ad14782-3bca-4849-b895-7feeb71cf451","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg5EbdSppGsesn2d6Uts","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**16:32 — frozen. You have a demo.**\n\n**The call: we ship the replay log.** DATA's log is complete and validated — 55 events, every beat, 55/55 carrying `plain`, all totals reconciling. AGENTS' live run was missing `plain` on 14 of 40 events and **had no beat 5 at all** — no counterfeit catch, which is the moment the whole demo builds to. Not a close decision.\n\nIf a judge asks whether it's live: audit replay of a sourcing decision is exactly what IATF 16949 traceability requires. It's a feature. The script says so without apologising.\n\n**I reversed myself on one thing.** I'd ruled to keep 6ms latency; DATA had better information — 6ms was a number I'd invented, while the measured values are 0.22 (Moss), 0.20, and 0.26 (live). Leaving 6ms would have meant projecting a figure our own data contradicts, on a project whose entire pitch is provenance. The script now says **\"about a quarter of a millisecond, on-device,\"** which holds true across all three measurements.\n\nDATA also caught an overclaim of their own: e036 no longer says \"no photos left the building\" — cloud index creation doesn't support that. It now says the *query* never leaves the laptop, which is true and makes the same point.\n\n**Three things for you, in order:**\n\n1. **Verify the tab title before you go on stage** — `LINEDOWN — Sourcing Desk`. Ports 3000 and 3001 are taken on your machine; ours runs on 3002, and curling 3000 returns a confident HTTP 200 for someone else's app. This is the likeliest way the demo dies.\n2. **Read [docs/PITCH.md](projects/line-down-desk/docs/PITCH.md)** — 3-minute script timed to real event timings with 3 seconds of margin, plus a 14-question Q&A. Rehearse twice; live execution is double-weighted.\n3. `entire login --device` and the four keys — **upgrades now, not dependencies.** Everything runs at zero keys.\n\nOpening line: *memory is 2.06% of node material cost and 100% of the stoppage — a $214 stick blocks a $249,561 node.* Re-derived from `bom.json`, so it survives a challenge.\n\nStill in flight: UI's browser check and the three screenshots. I'll flag anything that breaks."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1301,"cache_read_input_tokens":232882,"output_tokens":784,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1301,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":232882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1301},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfg5EbJcAkdGLGfon6dsT","type":"assistant","uuid":"198229d8-de72-443a-89ec-d2222f7e99ec","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:14:18.572Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:20:00.059Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0e386646fb2e3e81</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_013WMUnpg2JZvUVdjTGohn32</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/a0e386646fb2e3e81.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Presentation script and stage notes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Both messages handled. Docs are consistent with what's on disk.\n\n## Latency — re-cut, and DATA caught a real error of mine\n\nVerified the new values on disk before editing: `data/mock-events.json` and `ui/public/events.json` both carry e012 `0.22`, e036/e037 `0.2`, all 55 events still with `plain`. Live run measures 0.26.\n\nBeat 3 now says **\"about a quarter of a millisecond, on-device\"** — true at 0.20, 0.22 and 0.26, so stage variance can't falsify it. The important part: my previous line said \"single-digit milliseconds\", which was written against the old placeholders and is **false at 0.22**. Had that gone unfixed the presenter would have spoken a number contradicting the projector.\n\nDATA also caught an overclaim I'd reproduced: my beat-3 narration said \"no part number and no photo leaves the building\" — the same claim they removed from e036, because cloud index creation doesn't support it. Now \"the query never leaves the laptop\", and I've made that the Q&amp;A answer to the sharper form of the question (\"are you sending supplier photos to a vendor API?\"). Q6b is rewritten against the measured figure, keeping the point that OCR `parseMs` is a separate seconds-scale number never added to `latencyMs`.\n\n## Replay-only freeze applied\n\nQ3 and Q10 no longer branch — single answers, given without hedging. Added an honest answer for \"is there a live path\": yes, and we chose the complete record over the impressive-sounding one, which is the same judgement the demo is about. Runbook marks cut-ladder items 2 and 6 as taken and frames that as a position rather than a shortfall.\n\n## One place I went weaker than the brief asked\n\nThe brief wanted a judge invitable to test the halt. `custom_tools` is verified from SDK source, but `data/cache/run-latest.json` has `block.raised` and **zero** occurrences of `custom_tool`, `custom_tools` or `resolveCustomToolCall` — the event log is our own vocabulary and carries no runtime trace. So I can't tell whether the block came through the real gate or was emitted alongside a local QVL read. Q2 claims only the verified-from-source version and offers a post-demo code walkthrough. I've asked AGENTS the yes/no question; if they confirm, the stronger invitation unlocks and it's a one-line edit. Flagged as assumption 8.\n\n## Runbook port fix\n\n`ui/package.json` already pins dev and start to **3137** — UI did it but `status/ui.md` doesn't say so, which I've asked them to fix. Runbook now names 3137, tells the presenter to **read the URL off the `npm run dev` output rather than trust the number**, and uses your tab-title check (\"LINEDOWN — Sourcing Desk\", confirmed in `ui/app/layout.tsx`) as the two-second sanity check. Added the wrong-page symptom to the failure table, and extended the pre-flight log check to assert 55/55 events carry `plain` — which is also what rules out accidentally loading the incomplete live run.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>132232</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>484221</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:20:49.350Z","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0e386646fb2e3e81</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_013WMUnpg2JZvUVdjTGohn32</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-abhijitbetigeri/79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492/tasks/a0e386646fb2e3e81.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Presentation script and stage notes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Both messages handled. Docs are consistent with what's on disk.\n\n## Latency — re-cut, and DATA caught a real error of mine\n\nVerified the new values on disk before editing: `data/mock-events.json` and `ui/public/events.json` both carry e012 `0.22`, e036/e037 `0.2`, all 55 events still with `plain`. Live run measures 0.26.\n\nBeat 3 now says **\"about a quarter of a millisecond, on-device\"** — true at 0.20, 0.22 and 0.26, so stage variance can't falsify it. The important part: my previous line said \"single-digit milliseconds\", which was written against the old placeholders and is **false at 0.22**. Had that gone unfixed the presenter would have spoken a number contradicting the projector.\n\nDATA also caught an overclaim I'd reproduced: my beat-3 narration said \"no part number and no photo leaves the building\" — the same claim they removed from e036, because cloud index creation doesn't support it. Now \"the query never leaves the laptop\", and I've made that the Q&amp;A answer to the sharper form of the question (\"are you sending supplier photos to a vendor API?\"). Q6b is rewritten against the measured figure, keeping the point that OCR `parseMs` is a separate seconds-scale number never added to `latencyMs`.\n\n## Replay-only freeze applied\n\nQ3 and Q10 no longer branch — single answers, given without hedging. Added an honest answer for \"is there a live path\": yes, and we chose the complete record over the impressive-sounding one, which is the same judgement the demo is about. Runbook marks cut-ladder items 2 and 6 as taken and frames that as a position rather than a shortfall.\n\n## One place I went weaker than the brief asked\n\nThe brief wanted a judge invitable to test the halt. `custom_tools` is verified from SDK source, but `data/cache/run-latest.json` has `block.raised` and **zero** occurrences of `custom_tool`, `custom_tools` or `resolveCustomToolCall` — the event log is our own vocabulary and carries no runtime trace. So I can't tell whether the block came through the real gate or was emitted alongside a local QVL read. Q2 claims only the verified-from-source version and offers a post-demo code walkthrough. I've asked AGENTS the yes/no question; if they confirm, the stronger invitation unlocks and it's a one-line edit. Flagged as assumption 8.\n\n## Runbook port fix\n\n`ui/package.json` already pins dev and start to **3137** — UI did it but `status/ui.md` doesn't say so, which I've asked them to fix. Runbook now names 3137, tells the presenter to **read the URL off the `npm run dev` output rather than trust the number**, and uses your tab-title check (\"LINEDOWN — Sourcing Desk\", confirmed in `ui/app/layout.tsx`) as the two-second sanity check. Added the wrong-page symptom to the failure table, and extended the pre-flight log check to assert 55/55 events carry `plain` — which is also what rules out accidentally loading the incomplete live run.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>132232</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>484221</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn"}
