{"parentUuid":"2615b125-6f5a-4e21-a6f4-67a3cfa9fa94","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg5macJYDNQsevwxdDLT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You already have a repo — `line-down-desk`, private, pushed. You don't need a new one; `gh repo rename` keeps history and the remote.\n\n**Timing caveat first:** it's 16:35, submission 17:00. A product rename touches the UI `<title>`, README, and PITCH.md — and the tab title is your stage safety check against the port collision. Renaming the *repo* is free; renaming the *product* costs ~10 minutes and some risk.\n\nHere's how I'd weigh the candidates:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":832,"cache_read_input_tokens":234183,"output_tokens":2485,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1365},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":832,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2485,"cache_read_input_tokens":234183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":832},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfg5mZDhof48VmPzXepcN","type":"assistant","uuid":"91ff8ea2-74cc-4f45-8a12-1fd3abf2f5cd","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:21:31.801Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/Users/abhijitbetigeri","sessionId":"79c3b8a7-06a2-4fb1-8964-a4968e4c0492","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"dreamy-hugging-sutton"}
{"parentUuid":"91ff8ea2-74cc-4f45-8a12-1fd3abf2f5cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg5macJYDNQsevwxdDLT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WdNkU4JwvWkEEqCSmnyoZc","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Which name do you want for the project?","header":"Name","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"SecondSource","description":"'Second sourcing' is the exact industry term for qualifying an alternate supplier for a part — precisely what the product does. Insiders nod; outsiders still parse it. Strongest name, but costs ~10 min to propagate.","preview":"SECONDSOURCE\nrepo: second-source\n\n\"Second sourcing\" — the real procurement term for\nqualifying an alternate supplier.\n\n+ Industry-accurate; the one expert in the room nods\n+ Describes the solution, not the problem\n+ Positive framing\n- 10 min to propagate (UI title, README, PITCH)\n- Changes your tab-title safety check"},{"label":"LINEDOWN (keep)","description":"Current name. Real industry jargon for a production stoppage, matches the money-counter urgency, and already wired through UI title, README, pitch script and repo. Zero risk, zero minutes.","preview":"LINEDOWN\nrepo: line-down-desk  (already live)\n\n\"The sourcing desk that keeps the line running.\"\n\n+ Zero work, zero risk, 25 min from submission\n+ Real jargon; conveys urgency\n+ Already in UI title, README, PITCH, repo\n- Names the problem, not the solution\n- Slightly generic as a GitHub repo name"},{"label":"Qualified","description":"One word, and it is the crux of the entire demo — the block is about qualification, not specs. The cheapest part is blocked because it was never tested in that board.","preview":"QUALIFIED\nrepo: qualified\n\nThe whole demo in one word: the cheapest part is\nelectrically fine and still blocked, because it was\nnever tested in this board.\n\n+ Points straight at beat 4, the pivotal moment\n+ Short, memorable, good for People's Choice\n- Vague without context\n- Common word; weak GitHub uniqueness"},{"label":"Clearline","description":"Positive inversion of LINEDOWN — keeping the line clear rather than naming the failure. Reads well as a product, close enough to the current name that propagation is low-risk.","preview":"CLEARLINE\nrepo: clearline\n\nKeeping the line clear, rather than naming the failure.\n\n+ Product-sounding; positive framing\n+ Close to current name, low-risk rename\n+ Distinct on GitHub\n- Less industry-specific than SecondSource\n- Loses the urgency LINEDOWN carries"}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":832,"cache_read_input_tokens":234183,"output_tokens":2485,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1365},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":832,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2485,"cache_read_input_tokens":234183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":832},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WdNkU4JwvWkEEqCSmnyoZc":{"questions":[{"question":"Which name do you want for the project?","header":"Name","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"SecondSource","description":"'Second sourcing' is the exact industry term for qualifying an alternate supplier for a part — precisely what the product does. Insiders nod; outsiders still parse it. Strongest name, but costs ~10 min to propagate.","preview":"SECONDSOURCE\nrepo: second-source\n\n\"Second sourcing\" — the real procurement term for\nqualifying an alternate supplier.\n\n+ Industry-accurate; the one expert in the room nods\n+ Describes the solution, not the problem\n+ Positive framing\n- 10 min to propagate (UI title, README, PITCH)\n- Changes your tab-title safety check"},{"label":"LINEDOWN (keep)","description":"Current name. Real industry jargon for a production stoppage, matches the money-counter urgency, and already wired through UI title, README, pitch script and repo. Zero risk, zero minutes.","preview":"LINEDOWN\nrepo: line-down-desk  (already live)\n\n\"The sourcing desk that keeps the line running.\"\n\n+ Zero work, zero risk, 25 min from submission\n+ Real jargon; conveys urgency\n+ Already in UI title, README, PITCH, repo\n- Names the problem, not the solution\n- Slightly generic as a GitHub repo name"},{"label":"Qualified","description":"One word, and it is the crux of the entire demo — the block is about qualification, not specs. The cheapest part is blocked because it was never tested in that board.","preview":"QUALIFIED\nrepo: qualified\n\nThe whole demo in one word: the cheapest part is\nelectrically fine and still blocked, because it was\nnever tested in this board.\n\n+ Points straight at beat 4, the pivotal moment\n+ Short, memorable, good for People's Choice\n- Vague without context\n- Common word; weak GitHub uniqueness"},{"label":"Clearline","description":"Positive inversion of LINEDOWN — keeping the line clear rather than naming the failure. Reads well as a product, close enough to the current name that propagation is low-risk.","preview":"CLEARLINE\nrepo: clearline\n\nKeeping the line clear, rather than naming the failure.\n\n+ Product-sounding; positive framing\n+ Close to current name, low-risk rename\n+ Distinct on GitHub\n- Less industry-specific than SecondSource\n- Loses the urgency LINEDOWN carries"}]}]}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfg5mZDhof48VmPzXepcN","type":"assistant","uuid":"d412f3de-b440-43ce-a03a-7287766c361c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:21:43.108Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external",